{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check\ncat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\ngit status --short'","aggregated_output":"# Radix-4 sequential divider\n\nImplemented the proposed local arithmetic change in `rtl/div_unit.sv`.\nEach of the four recurrence cycles now contains four radix-4 steps. Each\nstep forms a 34-bit trial remainder and performs three independent\n35-bit unsigned subtractions. Borrow bits produce mutually exclusive\ndigit enables, and a masked parallel mux selects the next remainder.\nPREP registers unsigned 34-bit D, 2D and 3D from the current captured\ndivisor magnitude, with widening before shifts. No division or modulo\noperators were added.\n\nThe interface, eight states, original operand capture, signed correction,\noverflow and divide-by-zero handling, DONE backpressure, reset behavior,\nALTOPS constants/formulas and nret=1 pipeline are unchanged. The real\ndatapath remains excluded in ALTOPS builds. No architectural deviations.\n\nPreserved all existing tests. Added directed quotient-digit patterns,\nboundary vectors around D/2D/3D/4D, large divisor multiple-width cases,\nall sign combinations and operations, 6,000 fixed-seed operand pairs\n(24,000 randomized operations per arithmetic mode), and requests/early\nacceptance while busy. Existing helpers check exact completion on service\nedge 7, acceptance on edge 8, held results, immediate following requests,\nand reset cancellation in every phase against an independent integer\nreference.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Required Verilator lint command: passed without warnings.\n- `make test TARGET=bench`: all 9 runners passed, including real and\n  ALTOPS divider/pipeline builds and the no-combinational-divider check.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: passed selftest RVFI comparison with\n  and without stalls and canonical CoreMark CRC validation (2 ELFs).\n  The initial plain make invocation defaulted its C++ harness to NRET=2;\n  setting its existing NRET environment parameter to the core's declared\n  value fixed the build. No harness or contract files were changed.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=8 bash formal/run_all.sh`:\n  **PASS: 53 passed, 0 failed**, including unchanged liveness and the\n  register check. Passed on the first attempt; no fixes or retries.\n- `make timing TARGET=bench`: placement 0 passed at 41.665 MHz, 33 logic\n  levels, 3,274 logic cells and 697 registers. Worst reported arrival is\n  29.295 ns, quotient to remainder inside div_unit (baseline 37.205 ns).\n- `NRET=1 make fpga TARGET=bench`: passed all three placements at\n  41.665 / 42.390 / 42.390 MHz, median **42.390 MHz**. Canonical CoreMark\n  completed 10 iterations in **4,491,485 bracketed cycles**, unchanged\n  from the baseline, with fitness **94.38 iterations/s**, above the\n  71.7033 acceptance target. Median frequency improves approximately\n  37.68% over the recorded 30.789 MHz baseline.\n\nThe remaining timing limit in placement 0 is still the divider recurrence.\nParallel subtraction increases area versus the recorded baseline's 3,021\nlogic cells and 664 registers (approximately +8.37% logic and +4.97%\nregisters). PREP did not become the measured worst path.\nFast formal uses ALTOPS; actual arithmetic is covered by direct divider\nsimulation, pipeline simulation and cosimulation. Deep formal was not run.\n M cores/bench/rtl/div_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_div_unit.py\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
