{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_54", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check\ngit status --short\ncat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'", "aggregated_output": " M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n# Implementation\n\nImplemented the bounded four-source prediction in `forward_unit.sv`: each\nraw operand selects captured RF, EX/MEM ALU, MEM/WB ALU, or MEM/WB load.\nSelections include decoded write intent, nonzero destination matching and\nyoungest-writer priority before the existing ID/EX boundary. MEM exposes its\nresolved alignment/write permission, preventing a known faulting load from\nbecoming a predicted WB writer. WB's architectural write-data mux is unchanged.\n\nEX uses these registered sources directly in its parallel raw and ALU masks,\nwith local PC/immediate substitution. Actual EX/MEM and retained MEM/WB write\npermissions feed a separate validation cone. A failed selection bubbles the\nconsumer, suppresses M launch and branch training, flushes younger tokens and\nredirects to the consumer PC independently of instruction-bus readiness. Reset\nwins and an older dmem hold defers replay. M operands are verified before launch;\nthe existing snapshots, arithmetic, latency and completion protocol are unchanged.\nSelectors hold with dmem and migrate EX sources into WB while M drains older work.\nOperand validity is separate from the stall/reset-qualified replay request, so\ninternal bubble/wait controls do not repeat the replay request's qualification.\nM launch directly requires validated source permissions.\n\nNo pipeline stage, register-file port, predictor table, arithmetic change, public\nIO change, nret change or evaluation-file change was introduced. Existing hazard\nlogic needs no change because replay deasserts execute_wait before asserting the\nexisting correction/flush interface. There are no architectural deviations.\n\nAdded three pipeline tests with an independent retirement oracle checking all\nraw RVFI fields, exact traps/PC/order, accepted memory requests, validated M\nlaunches, competing writers, all four sources, known load faults, JAL/JALR\ncancellati\n…[1160 of 4232 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:57e63fd65b7137ee]…\ntools.eval.gowin bench --all-options`: all three unchanged\n  placement options completed. Final Fmax is 68.070 / 73.869 / 73.869 MHz;\n  median 73.869 MHz. Vendor resource counts: 5,310 logic, 1,929 registers,\n  zero LUT-RAM, four BSRAM, two DSPs. Median-option critical paths now start\n  at a registered forwarding selector and cross EX control/fetch/decode.\n- Final measured product: 73.869e6 * 10 / 4,037,538 = 182.9555536 iterations/s,\n  a 5.4157% improvement over 70.074 MHz at the same canonical cycle count.\n  This exceeds the stated 4.6% acceptance threshold and the 5% forecast.\n\nAll required local correctness gates pass. The timing spread is material:\nplacement option 0 is slower than the champion, while the required median\nimproves. These results use the existing three options without flow changes;\nthe orchestrator's independent final gates remain authoritative. No deep real\nM formal run was needed because the arithmetic units are untouched; their real\nand ALTOPS unit tests and real RVFI cosim all passed.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
