{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r11s0.yaml; tail -65 cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20261003-001-r11s0.log'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261003-001-r11s0\ntitle: \"Remove squash control from decode payload and forwarding-mask registers\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 182.96 iterations/s at 73.869 MHz and 4,037,538\n  bracket cycles. Its reported worst path runs from an EX/MEM result\n  through execute recovery and decode to a forwarding-select register.\n  Registered source prediction shortened operand selection, but its\n  eight source-mask flops still clear on flush_id, and ID/EX still clears\n  its complete payload on flush or invalid fetch. This broadcasts late\n  branch recovery into state whose contents are irrelevant for bubbles.\n  Earlier r3 validity-only work preceded the registered forwarding masks\n  and achieved gains below that round's winner. Recent comparator,\n  counter-update and divider changes failed to beat the current champion.\n  Revisit the specific control fanout at the new measured endpoint.\nhypothesis: |\n  Factor ID/EX squashing into the instruction-valid bit alone, removing\n  flush and fetch validity from decode payload and registered forwarding\n  source-mask updates. This is one local control-fanout optimization.\n  Preserve all stage boundaries, instruction latencies, fetch behavior,\n  branch recovery timing, source priority and M-unit schedules.\n\n  In id_stage split valid from the remaining payload assignments. For\n  valid preserve exactly reset/flush priority, then stall hold, otherwise\n  capture in.valid. For every other field reset to zero, hold on stall,\n  otherwise capture the raw decoded instruction, register values and\n  metadata regardless of flush or in.valid. Do not clear payload on a\n  bubble and do not gate its enable with decode_accept: that would restore\n  the redirect dependency. A load-use flush with stall retains the old\n  payload but invalidates it; an unstalled redirect may capture wrong-path\n  payload with valid zero. Neither is an executing instruction.\n\n  In forward_unit reset source masks as before, but remove flush_id and\n  id_valid from their sequential update conditions\n…[96508 of 99580 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:59c36cbffb94d194]…\ntmp/561ff4c6/7ebaeff3/r11s0-masklifecycle/pipeline.log; tail -3 /srv/hwebench/tmp/561ff4c6/7ebaeff3/r11s0-masklifecycle/cosim-build.log'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_62\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -c 'tail -5 /srv/hwebench/tmp/561ff4c6/7ebaeff3/r11s0-masklifecycle/pipeline.log; tail -3 /srv/hwebench/tmp/561ff4c6/7ebaeff3/r11s0-masklifecycle/cosim-build.log'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"..                                                                       [100%]\\n2 passed, 2 deselected in 6.38s\\n- Verilator: Built from 0.820 MB sources in 16 modules, into 0.523 MB in 7 C++ files needing 0.001 MB\\n- Verilator: Walltime 4.239 s (elab=0.006, cvt=0.036, bld=4.186); cpu 0.054 s on 1 threads; allocated 26.055 MB\\nBuilt: /srv/hwebench/tmp/561ff4c6/7ebaeff3/r11s0-masklifecycle/obj_dir/cosim_sim\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\nsudo: cannot execute '/usr/local/sbin/hwe-agent-scope': Broken pipe (os error 32)\nKilled\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
