{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg --files -uu cores/bench/experiments | rg -v '/hypotheses/|\\\\.png\"'$'\"' | head -60; tail -3 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "cores/bench/experiments/.gitkeep\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\ncores/bench/experiments/run_summary.json\ncores/bench/experiments/.scribe.log\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-001-r10s0\", \"title\": \"Sign-biased parallel halfword branch comparison\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The champion scores 182.96 iterations/s at 73.869 MHz and 4,037,538 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its reported worst path passes through execute, fetch and decode, while other placements expose the divider. Recent branch-recovery predecoding and retiming candidates regressed. The proposed local change targets the comparison datapath feeding same-cycle branch resolution. It leaves recovery controls, predictor policy and pipeline timing intact.\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The champion scores 182.96 iterations/s at 73.869 MHz and 4,037,538 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its reported worst path passes through execute, fetch and decode, while other placements expose the divider. Recent branch-recovery predecoding and retiming candidates regressed. The proposed local change targets the comparison datapath feeding same-cycle branch resolution. It leaves recovery controls, predictor policy and pipeline timing intact.\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the EX branch comparison network with one signedness-biased comparator built from two parallel 16-bit comparisons. For ordered branches, branch_op[1] distinguishes signed BLT/BGE (zero) from unsigned BLTU/BGEU (one). Form high operands HA={rs1[31] XOR !branch_op[1],rs1[30:16]} and HB={rs2[31] XOR !branch_op[1],rs2[30:16]}. Inverting both sign bits maps signed order exactly into unsigned order; leave them unchanged for unsigned branches. Calculate hi_lt=(HA<HB), hi_eq=(rs1[31:16]==rs2[31:16]), and lo_lt=(rs1[15:0]<rs2[15:0]) independently with native short unsigned comparisons. Then ordered_lt=hi_lt OR (hi_eq AND lo_lt). Equality is hi_eq AND (rs1[15:0]==rs2[15:0]). No full-width carry-dependent comparison or late signed-versus-unsigned result mux is needed.\\n\\nSelect primitive = branch_op[2] ? ordered_lt : equality\n…[34333 of 37405 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5cf90014652db9ed]…\nB transfer boundary. Preserve the existing comparisons, pre-edge semantics and all architectural assertions. Add actually-untaken ordered branches whose narrow result says taken but whose direct targets overflow, underflow or cross the one-megabyte boundary; assert no speculative out-of-range fetch.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 174.25, \"delta_pct\": -4.76, \"vs_baseline\": 1337.71, \"fmax_mhz\": 70.668, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4055597, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5425, \"ff\": 1973, \"seeds\": [69.291, 70.668, 70.668], \"perturbations\": [[0, 69.291, 18], [1, 70.668, 18], [2, 70.668, 18]], \"lutram\": 0, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/quotient_31_s1\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/remainder_24_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -9.432, \"arrival_ns\": 19.726, \"logic_cells\": 73, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_div\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 18, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T11:06:47.504351Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 10}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
