ur-way source masks, producer priority and canceled-write replay. Keep branch_taken, alignment faults, actual_taken, redirect qualification and target selection, training, PC arithmetic and RVFI next-PC logic unchanged. This is a combinational arithmetic micro-optimization, not a different predictor or a deferred branch check.\n\nIn alu.sv use the same two-half relation for SLTU and sign-corrected relation for SLT. Continue comparing the actual selected a/b inputs, including sign-extended immediates. Leave addition, subtraction, shifts, bitwise operations, M arithmetic, all operation encodings and the combinational ALU interface unchanged. Share the unsigned relation within each consumer rather than describing independent signed and unsigned full-width subtractor cones. Do not merge branch and ALU operand streams, narrow architectural operands, assume memory bounds for arithmetic, or insert any register.\n\nPreserve all reset, flush, invalid-bubble, dmem hold, load-use, M-unit service and completion behavior, nret=1 external IO and RVFI retirement ordering. Decoder legality, misalignment traps, suppression of memory side effects, full-width targets and all evaluation contracts remain unchanged. Every comparison is exact for arbitrary 32-bit values, including opposite signs and equal high halves.\n\nAdd independent-reference checks for all branch predicates and SLT/SLTU/SLTI/SLTIU. Exercise equal operands, differences confined to either half, first differing bit at positions 15/16/30/31, 0x0000ffff versus 0x00010000, INT_MIN, INT_MAX, negative immediates and opposing signed/unsigned order. Cover every forwarding source, retained WB data during memory holds, taken/not-taken saved predictions, misaligned taken and untaken targets, cancellation replay, reset and once-only retirement. Retain all existing assertions and run unchanged real/ALTOPS pipeline, ALU, formal and stalled RVFI cosimulation checks plus canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/marker validation.\n\nExpect unchanged 4,037,538 bracket cycles with identical instruction and stall streams. Forecast five percent fitness improvement with low confidence, entirely from Fmax. Acceptance requires more than 191.37616 iterations/s, approximately 77.27 MHz at that cycle count. Gowin may already optimize full-width comparisons, the high-equality merge may add routing delay, and the divider or ALU-result paths may cap the benefit. The earlier eight-bit-sliced comparator mentioned in r9s2 measured only 62.743 MHz median; this deliberately uses two larger halves to avoid its multi-group merge depth, but that negative evidence still limits confidence. Judge the complete prescribed vendor median, not RTL operator counts or a single favorable placement. No gain is claimed before those measurements.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':5,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Compute shared exact equality, unsigned less-than and signed less-than relations from two parallel 16-bit halves of forwarded rs1/rs2; substitute them into the existing six branch predicates. Preserve default false decoding, every branch/replay/trap/redirect/training control and all pipeline behavior.'},\n{'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'Use the same exact parallel-halfword unsigned comparator and sign correction for SLTU and SLT, sharing the relation within the ALU. Preserve inputs, op encodings, all other arithmetic and both real/ALTOPS M-extension branches.'},\n{'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'Retain all existing arithmetic tests; add independent signed/unsigned comparison cases stressing equal high halves, cross-half boundaries, opposite signs and bit 31. Keep every M-extension check intact.'},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Add focused branch and comparison-immediate coverage at halfword/sign boundaries, including all forwarded operand sources, saved prediction directions, backpressure, replay and alignment traps. Preserve existing progress, latency, flush and RVFI assertions.'}\n]}\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=90))\nprint('Wrote and validated',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Wrote and validated cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r10s0.yaml\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
