{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nids={'hyp-20261003-001-r3s0','hyp-20261003-002-r3s1','hyp-20261003-001-r7s0','hyp-20261003-001-r8s0','hyp-20261003-001-r10s0'}\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id'] in ids:\n  print('\\\\nID:',d['id'])\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print(h.get('hypothesis',h) if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('NOTES:',d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nids={'hyp-20261003-001-r3s0','hyp-20261003-002-r3s1','hyp-20261003-001-r7s0','hyp-20261003-001-r8s0','hyp-20261003-001-r10s0'}\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id'] in ids:\n  print('\\\\nID:',d['id'])\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print(h.get('hypothesis',h) if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('NOTES:',d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\nID: hyp-20261003-001-r3s0\nMake pipeline bubbles depend on the existing ID/EX valid bit rather than\nclearing or masking the whole decode payload. This is a local control\nfactoring optimization: retain the pipeline stages, branch resolution\ncycle, forwarding priorities, memory handshake and divider schedule.\n\nIn if_stage, drive out.instr directly from imem_data even on flush or\nredirect. Retain out.valid = !(flush || redirect), the current PC update\npriorities, and the unchanged imem address interface. Decoding invalid\nor wrong-path instruction bits is harmless only when validity guards\nevery downstream consumer with architectural or interlock effects.\n\nIn id_stage, separate the ID/EX valid register update from every other\npayload field. Keep reset initialization. Update pc, instruction, source\nvalues/addresses, immediate, destination and decoded controls only when\n!stall; flush must not clear, select, or inhibit these payload updates.\nUpdate valid with reset/flush priority over stall: clear on reset or\nflush, hold on stall, otherwise capture in.valid. In particular a\nload-use bubble clears valid while retaining the stalled old payload;\na redirect can capture arbitrary raw wrong-path payload with valid=0.\nDo not introduce an in.valid-conditioned payload mux that recreates the\nsame redirect-to-data path. Do not change the decoder's default-illegal\ndiscipline or its interpretation of any instruction encoding.\n\nQualify the hazard unit's ID/EX load indication with id_ex_w.valid at\nthe core connection. This is essential because an invalid bubble may\nnow retain mem_read=1 and a nonzero destination from an earlier load.\nKeep raw IF instruction source fields independent of redirect; their\nincidental matches during an unavailable fetch cannot advance the PC\nbecause imem_ready already stalls it. Keep redirect priority over PC\nstall. Preserve dmem/execute hold priority over ID flushing. Audit every\nconsumer of ID/EX controls: EX already qualifies division and redirect\nwith in.valid, and clears the entire EX/MEM bundle on !in\n…[19391 of 22463 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:780cd159284c1cd3]…\nan; this deliberately uses two larger halves to avoid its multi-group merge depth, but that negative evidence still limits confidence. Judge the complete prescribed vendor median, not RTL operator counts or a single favorable placement. No gain is claimed before those measurements.\n\nA precursor with parallel 16/16 comparisons followed by a late signed-result mux measured 75.402 MHz in vendor placement option 1, with 5,258 LUT4 and 1,929 registers. Its unchanged CoreMark validator passed canonical CRCs, validation text, bounded accesses, markers and exactly 4,037,538 cycles. This precursor is below the acceptance threshold and is not evidence of a win. The final proposal moves signedness handling to the high-half input and folds branch inversion into the common primitive, removing further late selection logic. Timing of this complete refinement remains to be established; the five-percent estimate is speculative. All experiments use scratch RTL outside the repository; only this hypothesis is delivered.\nNOTES: \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
