{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_34", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in ['hyp-20261003-003-r9s2','hyp-20261003-002-r9s1','hyp-20261003-001-r9s0']:\n  print(d['id']); print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261003-001-r9s0\nImplement the existing 64 two-bit bimodal counters as 64 constant-index generated register words, each with its own training enable and explicit Boolean saturating transition. Preserve the same table size, indexing, state encoding, initialization, lookup and training edge. This is a micro-optimization of the existing state-update circuit, not a predictor-policy change, a new predictor or delayed training.\n\nFor entry i, use enable_i = branch_train && (branch_index == i), comparing at exactly six bits. Let h=counters[i][1], l=counters[i][0] and t=branch_outcome. On an enabled update, assign next_h = (h && l) || (t && (h || l)); next_l = (h && !l) || (t && (h || !l)). Each next-state bit is a three-input Boolean function of this entry's old state and outcome. Use elaboration-time constant indexing so there is no counters[branch_index] old-state read in the update datapath. Reset each entry synchronously to 01 with priority over training; otherwise hold every nonselected entry. Keep the dynamic counters[pc[7:2]][1] fetch lookup unchanged.\n\nThese equations implement taken transitions 00->01, 01->10, 10->11, 11->11 and not-taken transitions 00->00, 01->00, 10->01, 11->10. Preserve nonblocking assignment semantics: fetch and ID/EX must observe the pre-edge prediction on simultaneous same-index training. Every update uses the current entry state at resolution, never the counter value sampled when the instruction was fetched. Do not add write-through, reset scrubbing, forwarding of a newly trained direction, or an extra training register.\n\nKeep branch_train qualification, alias behavior, direct-target derivation and its full-width bounds/alignment checks exactly as today. Preserve the two-entry queue, fall-through bypass, redirect priority, stalls, raw decode, forwarding/replay, ALU and M units. Maintain nret=1, all public IO, exact traps, monotonic retirement, memory side-effect suppression, arithmetic correctness and symbolic progress. No evaluation or contract files change.\n\nThe intended benefit i\n…[13282 of 16354 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:cc5805b04449e019]…\nared ID/EX and zero source masks after squash, the original\nbranch-to-divider latency bound and formal liveness window. Run unchanged\nreal/ALTOPS pipeline tests, formal, stalled cosimulation and canonical\nCoreMark validation. Add focused relation/prediction coverage without\nweakening checks or modifying evaluation files.\n\nA scratch version with the predecoded predicates but still using generic\nEX-advancement qualification passed all 53 unchanged formal checks,\nall 37 existing pipeline tests in each real/ALTOPS mode, and canonical\nstalled CoreMark validation at 4,037,538 cycles. It measured\n71.018/72.154/72.154 MHz, median 72.154 MHz, with 5,304 LUT4 and 1,933\nregisters. This is approximately 178.71 iterations/s, BELOW the champion\nand acceptance threshold; it is not evidence of a demonstrated gain.\nThe specialized control-transfer qualification is an additional concrete\nrefinement beyond that tested version. The forecast is uncertain and\nrequires the implementation phase's full correctness and timing gates.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\ns=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/561ff4c6/7ebaeff3/r11s0-alumasks/rtl')\nshutil.copytree('cores/bench/rtl',s,dirs_exist_ok=True)\np=s/'id_stage.sv';t=p.read_text().replace('  output id_ex_t  out','  output logic alu_pc_select,\\\\n  output logic alu_imm_select,\\\\n  output id_ex_t  out')\nt=t.replace('  ctrl_t ctrl_decoded;', '  assign alu_pc_select = dec_is_auipc;\\\\n  assign alu_imm_select = dec_alu_src;\\\\n\\\\n  ctrl_t ctrl_decoded;')\np.write_text(t)\np=s/'forward_unit.sv';t=p.read_text().replace('  output logic [3:0] fwd_rs1,', '  input logic id_alu_pc,\\\\n  input logic id_alu_imm,\\\\n  output logic [4:0] alu_fwd1, alu_fwd2,\\\\n  output logic [3:0] fwd_rs1,')\ni=t.index('  // WB permission')\nnew='''  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (reset || flush_id) begin\n      alu_fwd1 <= '0;\n      alu_fwd2 <= '0;\n    end else if (stall_id) begin\n      if (\"'!stall_ex_mem) begin\n        alu_fwd1 <= {alu_fwd1[4], alu_fwd1[1] && ex_mem_load,\n                     alu_fwd1[1] && !ex_mem_load, 1'\"'b0,\n                     \"'!alu_fwd1[4] && !alu_fwd1[1]};\n        alu_fwd2 <= {alu_fwd2[4], alu_fwd2[1] && ex_mem_load,\n                     alu_fwd2[1] && !ex_mem_load, 1'\"'b0,\n                     \"'!alu_fwd2[4] && !alu_fwd2[1]};\n      end\n    end else if (!id_valid) begin\n      alu_fwd1 <= '\"'0;\n      alu_fwd2 <= '0;\n    end else begin\n      alu_fwd1 <= {id_alu_pc,\n                   \"'!id_alu_pc && rs1_wb && ex_mem_load,\n                   !id_alu_pc && rs1_wb && !ex_mem_load,\n                   !id_alu_pc && rs1_ex,\n                   !id_alu_pc && !(rs1_ex || rs1_wb)};\n      alu_fwd2 <= {id_alu_imm,\n                   !id_alu_imm && rs2_wb && ex_mem_load,\n                   !id_alu_imm && rs2_wb && !ex_mem_load,\n                   !id_alu_imm && rs2_ex,\n                   !id_alu_imm &