{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_24", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor s in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(s)\n if d['id'] in ['hyp-20261003-003-r9s2','hyp-20261003-002-r9s1']:\n  print(d['id'],d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261003-002-r9s1 Partition conditional-branch resolution into registered static control in ID and dynamic operand comparisons in EX. At the existing ID/EX capture edge, register one-hot controls for the six legal branch predicates, one-hot controls for the predicate that means the captured prediction is wrong, branch-training eligibility derived from direct target alignment, and the single correction destination implied by the captured prediction. This is one structural retiming of the branch-control boundary; it neither adds a pipeline stage nor changes prediction policy, fetch buffering, forwarding selection, ALU/M service schedules or retirement width.\n\nFor a validated branch, form six outcome enables for EQ, NE, signed LT, signed GE, unsigned LT and unsigned GE. For an aligned direct target, form the corresponding six recovery enables after XORing branch_op bit zero with this token's predicted_taken bit. Thus a predicted-not-taken BEQ requests correction on EQ, while a predicted-taken BEQ requests correction on NE; the same complementary pairing applies to signed and unsigned comparisons. All other recovery enables are zero. For a misaligned direct target, actual_taken must be false whether or not the comparison succeeds, so record a separate forced-fallthrough recovery bit equal to predicted_taken. Keep default-illegal decoding unchanged; nonbranches and invalid decode entries must not acquire branch enables.\n\nAlso register two mutually exclusive training classes for legal branches: aligned target, which can train for either outcome, and misaligned target, which may train only if the condition is false. The latter preserves the existing rule that an untaken branch does not fault merely because its encoded target is misaligned. Compute the target alignment from the full-width PC-plus-immediate semantics in ID. Do not truncate architectural targets or wrap addresses. Register one branch_recovery_target alongside this metadata: predicted_taken ? PC+4 : PC+branch_immediate. A direction correction for a cond\n…[10042 of 13114 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:8227890bc91c2433]…\nared ID/EX and zero source masks after squash, the original\nbranch-to-divider latency bound and formal liveness window. Run unchanged\nreal/ALTOPS pipeline tests, formal, stalled cosimulation and canonical\nCoreMark validation. Add focused relation/prediction coverage without\nweakening checks or modifying evaluation files.\n\nA scratch version with the predecoded predicates but still using generic\nEX-advancement qualification passed all 53 unchanged formal checks,\nall 37 existing pipeline tests in each real/ALTOPS mode, and canonical\nstalled CoreMark validation at 4,037,538 cycles. It measured\n71.018/72.154/72.154 MHz, median 72.154 MHz, with 5,304 LUT4 and 1,933\nregisters. This is approximately 178.71 iterations/s, BELOW the champion\nand acceptance threshold; it is not evidence of a demonstrated gain.\nThe specialized control-transfer qualification is an additional concrete\nrefinement beyond that tested version. The forecast is uncertain and\nrequires the implementation phase's full correctness and timing gates.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
