m\": 0,\n  \"bsram\": 4,\n  \"dsp\": 2,\n  \"critical_paths\": [\n    {\n      \"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.alu_result_4_s0\",\n      \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/head_q.instr_3_s0\",\n      \"slack_ns\": -8.662,\n      \"arrival_ns\": 18.956,\n      \"logic_cells\": 37,\n      \"modules\": [\n        \"clock_ibuf\",\n        \"cpu/u_ex\",\n        \"cpu/u_if\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.alu_result_4_s0\",\n      \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/head_q.instr_4_s0\",\n      \"slack_ns\": -8.662,\n      \"arrival_ns\": 18.956,\n      \"logic_cells\": 37,\n      \"modules\": [\n        \"clock_ibuf\",\n        \"cpu/u_ex\",\n        \"cpu/u_if\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.alu_result_4_s0\",\n      \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/pc_15_s1\",\n      \"slack_ns\": -8.661,\n      \"arrival_ns\": 18.955,\n      \"logic_cells\": 37,\n      \"modules\": [\n        \"clock_ibuf\",\n        \"cpu/u_ex\",\n        \"cpu/u_if\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.alu_result_4_s0\",\n      \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/pc_17_s1\",\n      \"slack_ns\": -8.661,\n      \"arrival_ns\": 18.955,\n      \"logic_cells\": 37,\n      \"modules\": [\n        \"clock_ibuf\",\n        \"cpu/u_ex\",\n        \"cpu/u_if\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.alu_result_4_s0\",\n      \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/tail_q.instr_3_s0\",\n      \"slack_ns\": -8.659,\n      \"arrival_ns\": 18.954,\n      \"logic_cells\": 37,\n      \"modules\": [\n        \"clock_ibuf\",\n        \"cpu/u_ex\",\n        \"cpu/u_if\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_37", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r12s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261003-001-r12s0',\n 'title':'Remove bubble clearing from wide decode and execute payload inputs',\n 'category':'micro_opt',\n 'motivation':'''The champion scores 182.96 iterations/s at 73.869 MHz with 4,037,538 CoreMark bracket cycles. Vendor timing reproduced the 73.869 MHz result and shows forwarding-mask to branch-recovery to ID/EX clear feedback; nearby candidates also become limited by ALU-to-memory paths. The r11 validity-only decode proposal changed ID/EX and forwarding masks but left EX/MEM's wide bubble clearing in place and regressed 1.32 percent. The r8 result-routing proposal retained inactive EX payload, requiring a bubble-dependent payload enable, and bundled other routing changes. The remaining opportunity is to remove bubble-dependent data gating at BOTH existing payload boundaries without changing the forwarding-mask implementation.''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Separate validity and side-effect controls from the wide ID/EX and EX/MEM payload update conditions. Let payload data capture whenever its stage is not held, even when the token is invalid, flushed or waiting for an M result. This is one control-fanout and input-mux micro-optimization applied consistently to the two existing execute-path register boundaries. There is no extra pipeline stage, changed instruction latency, new speculation policy or altered branch comparator.\n\nIn id_stage retain synchronous reset of the complete bundle. Otherwise update valid with the exact existing priorities: flush clears it even when stalled; stall retains it; ordinary capture takes in.valid. All other fields, including decoded controls, capture the current raw selected token whenever \"'!stall, independent of flush and in.valid. During stall they retain their previous values. Never introduce decode_accept or a bubble-dependent payload enable, since those would restore the late recovery path. Qualify the core hazard connection'\"'s id_ex_mem_read with id_ex_w.valid, because invalid ID/EX payload may contain a load. Retain the existing valid qualification on producer write intent and all executing-instruction consumers.\n\nIn ex_stage retain reset clearing and dmem-stall holding of the complete EX/MEM register. On every other edge capture ALL non-control payload fields unconditionally using their existing expressions: PC, ALU/M/link result, raw store operand, register addresses, forwarded RVFI operands, resolved PC/branch metadata and instruction. Independently, clear ctrl and valid when operands_invalid || execute_wait || \"'!in.valid; otherwise capture ctrl_with_trap and in.valid. Do not retain inactive payload on a bubble: that would put execute_wait, replay or validity back on its write enable. Valid and side-effect controls must still become zero on every bubble, replay and incomplete M operation. Early captures of an incomplete M result are harmless only with those controls and valid cleared; the actual completion edge still captures the correct held result and operand snapshots.\n\nKeep forward_unit completely unchanged, including reset/flush/invalid clearing of its four-way masks, dmem retention, M-wait aging, permission verification and canceled-write replay. Keep MEM/WB'\"'s retained forwarding payload and permission on data-bus stalls unchanged. Raw ID controls must never launch M work, request memory, redirect, train, write a register or retire when ID/EX.valid is false. EX/MEM's zero controls must keep memory requests and forwarding disabled despite its freely changing data. Preserve all existing stage priorities, decoder legality, x0, target and memory misalignment traps, full-width arithmetic, real/ALTOPS M schedules, nret=1 external IO and precise RVFI operands/order.\n\nThe mechanism is removal of wide reset/zero-select and bubble-enable cones rather than a reduction of branch work or instruction count. The r11 change removed only the first boundary and altered source-mask behavior; this proposal preserves those masks and also removes zero-selection before the registered ALU result that feeds memory and forwarding. The r8 approach held inactive EX payload instead of capturing it, so it did not remove its bubble-dependent enable. No dedicated address register, writeback merge, comparator rewrite or divider change is included.\n\nVerify architectural and control equivalence across load-use bubbles, imem/dmem holds, redirects, canceled-producer replay, M launch/wait/completion and reset. Include invalid ID tokens containing LOAD, STORE, branch, JALR and every M encoding, and younger memory/M instructions behind squashes. Assert exact zero EX/MEM side-effect controls on bubbles, no wrong-path memory acceptance/M launch, retained WB forwarding, exact RVFI state and once-only retirement. Tests which inspect a completely zero invalid payload must instead check validity, zero EX/MEM side-effect controls and absence of architectural effects; do not relax decoder, arithmetic, ordering, progress or latency checks. Run unchanged formal and reference-ISS cosimulation plus canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/marker validation. Expect exactly 4,037,538 bracket cycles under identical input and stall streams.\n\nForecast seven percent fitness gain with low confidence, entirely from Fmax. Acceptance requires more than 191.37616 iterations/s, about 77.27 MHz at unchanged cycles. The divider recurrence, remaining forwarding-mask clear fanout, added payload switching or vendor placement can prevent the gain. The estimate is a hypothesis, not an achieved score; judge the complete prescribed Gowin placement median. Deliver only this hypothesis file; scratch prototypes do not alter repository RTL.''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':7,'confidence':'low'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Split valid update from all other ID/EX fields. Preserve reset and exact valid flush/hold priorities; capture payload whenever not stalled, independent of fetch validity and flush.'},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Split EX/MEM ctrl/valid bubble handling from payload writes. Preserve reset and dmem hold. On all other edges capture wide payload unconditionally; clear only ctrl/valid for replay, incomplete M work or an invalid EX token.'},\n {'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'Qualify the hazard-unit ID/EX load indication with id_ex_w.valid. Preserve existing valid-qualified producer intent, forwarding interfaces and nret=1 ports.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Add invalid-payload and once-only side-effect checks across flush, load-use, bus holds, replay, M waits/completion and reset. Update only invalid-token representation checks to examine valid and side-effect controls instead of irrelevant data bits. Preserve every architectural, arithmetic, RVFI, progress and latency assertion.'}\n ]}\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=90))\nprint('Rewritten and schema-validated',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_37", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r12s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261003-001-r12s0',\n 'title':'Remove bubble clearing from wide decode and execute payload inputs',\n 'category':'micro_opt',\n 'motivation':'''The champion scores 182.96 iterations/s at 73.869 MHz with 4,037,538 CoreMark bracket cycles. Vendor timing reproduced the 73.869 MHz result and shows forwarding-mask to branch-recovery to ID/EX clear feedback; nearby candidates also become limited by ALU-to-memory paths. The r11 validity-only decode proposal changed ID/EX and forwarding masks but left EX/MEM's wide bubble clearing in place and regressed 1.32 percent. The r8 result-routing proposal retained inactive EX payload, requiring a bubble-dependent payload enable, and bundled other routing changes. The remaining opportunity is to remove bubble-dependent data gating at BOTH existing payload boundaries without changing the forwarding-mask implementation.''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Separate validity and side-effect controls from the wide ID/EX and EX/MEM payload update conditions. Let payload data capture whenever its stage is not held, even when the token is invalid, flushed or waiting for an M result. This is one control-fanout and input-mux micro-optimization applied consistently to the two existing execute-path register boundaries. There is no extra pipeline stage, changed instruction latency, new speculation policy or altered branch comparator.\n\nIn id_stage retain synchronous reset of the complete bundle. Otherwise update valid with the exact existing priorities: flush clears it even when stalled; stall retains it; ordinary capture takes in.valid. All other fields, including decoded controls, capture the current raw selected token whenever \"'!stall, independent of flush and in.valid. During stall they