{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '50,125p' /srv/hwebench/tmp/561ff4c6/a0b518c6/r12s0/lean_all/if_stage.sv; sed -n '143,188p' /srv/hwebench/tmp/561ff4c6/a0b518c6/r12s0/lean_all/id_stage.sv; rg -n 'payload_dequeue' /srv/hwebench/tmp/561ff4c6/a0b518c6/r12s0/lean_all/core.sv\"","aggregated_output":"  assign dequeue = decode_accept && out.valid && !reset && !redirect;\n  assign bus_token = {pc, imem_data, predict_taken};\n  assign selected = occupancy != 0 ? head_q : bus_token;\n\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (reset || redirect) begin\n      // Occupancy invalidates both complete tokens. Payload flops retain\n      // don't-care data, avoiding a correction/reset mux on every bit.\n      occupancy <= 0;\n    end else begin\n      case (occupancy)\n        0: if (fetch_accept && !dequeue) begin\n          occupancy <= 1;\n        end\n        1: begin\n          if (dequeue) begin\n            if (!fetch_accept) occupancy <= 0;\n          end else if (fetch_accept) begin\n            occupancy <= 2;\n          end\n        end\n        2: if (dequeue) begin\n          occupancy <= 1;\n        end\n        default: occupancy <= 0;\n      endcase\n    end\n  end\n\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    case (occupancy)\n      0: head_q <= bus_token;\n      1: begin\n        if (payload_dequeue) head_q <= bus_token;\n        tail_q <= bus_token;\n      end\n      2: if (payload_dequeue) head_q <= tail_q;\n      default: ;\n    endcase\n  end\n\n  always_comb begin\n    direct_branch = imem_data[6:0] == 7'b1100011 &&\n                    (imem_data[14:12] == 3'd0 || imem_data[14:12] == 3'd1 ||\n                     imem_data[14:12] == 3'd4 || imem_data[14:12] == 3'd5 ||\n                     imem_data[14:12] == 3'd6 || imem_data[14:12] == 3'd7);\n    direct_jump = imem_data[6:0] == 7'b1101111;\n    direct_imm = direct_jump\n               ? {{11{imem_data[31]}}, imem_data[31], imem_data[19:12],\n                  imem_data[20], imem_data[30:21], 1'b0}\n               : {{19{imem_data[31]}}, imem_data[31], imem_data[7],\n                  imem_data[30:25], imem_data[11:8], 1'b0};\n    // Check the full sum, including carry/negative high bits. Never wrap\n    // a target into the one-megabyte executable region.\n    direct_target = pc + direct_imm;\n    predict_taken = (direct_jump || (direct_branch && counters[pc[7:2]][1]))\n                    && pc[1:0] == 2'b00 && pc[31:20] == 12'b0\n                    && direct_target[1:0] == 2'b00\n                    && direct_target[31:20] == 12'b0;\n    next_pc = predict_taken ? direct_target : pc + 32'd4;\n  end\n\n  // EX emits corrections only when it advances. They override even an\n  // unready instruction bus; otherwise PC advances only on bus acceptance.\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if      (reset)    pc <= RESET_PC;\n    else if (redirect) pc <= redirect_target;\n    else if (fetch_accept) pc <= next_pc;\n  end\n\n  // Nonblocking updates intentionally give both the PC mux and ID/EX\n  // the pre-edge lookup, including simultaneous same-index training.\n  // Resolve against the current entry, never a snapshot from fetch.\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (reset) begin\n      for (int i = 0; i < 64; i++) counters[i] <= 2'b01;\n84:  logic       payload_dequeue;\n109:    .payload_dequeue (payload_dequeue),\n203:    .payload_dequeue(payload_dequeue),\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_40", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r12s0.yaml');d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Remove squash and bubble control from wide pipeline payload updates'\nd['hypothesis']=d['hypothesis'].replace('ID/EX and EX/MEM payload update conditions','fetch-queue, ID/EX and EX/MEM payload update conditions').replace('the two existing execute-path register boundaries','the existing payload register boundaries')\nneedle='Keep forward_unit completely unchanged'\npos=d['hypothesis'].index(needle)\nd['hypothesis']=d['hypothesis'][:pos]+'''Apply the same separation to IF queue payloads. The queue already invalidates tokens through occupancy, but its payload assignments are still inside the reset/redirect branch and depend on redirect-qualified fetch_accept/dequeue. Export a payload_dequeue permission from hazard_unit equal to head_valid && \"'!load_use_hazard && !dmem_stall && !execute_wait, without redirect. Keep architectural decode_accept = payload_dequeue && !redirect exactly equivalent to today. This permission is ONLY a payload-write hint; it must never pop occupancy, advance PC, acknowledge a fetch, or admit a real instruction by itself.\n\nPreserve the queue occupancy state machine, true fetch_accept/dequeue equations, PC update and redirect/reset priorities exactly. Move head_q/tail_q writes into a separate clocked block: when old occupancy is zero, capture bus_token into head_q unconditionally; when it is one, capture bus_token into tail_q unconditionally and into head_q only on payload_dequeue; when it is two, copy tail_q into head_q only on payload_dequeue and retain tail_q. No payload write is gated by redirect, reset, imem_ready or true decode_accept. For each token that becomes live, the unchanged occupancy transition guarantees that the correct ready-bus token or old tail was captured. Writes to unoccupied or just-squashed slots are unobservable. Preserve complete PC/instruction/predicted_taken token coherence, two-entry capacity, conservative full-queue behavior and pre-edge predictor lookup. This specifically removes the residual recovery-to-fetch-payload-enable path exposed after the ID/EX and EX/MEM refinement.\n\n'\"''' + d['hypothesis'][pos:]\nd['hypothesis'] += '''\n\nA scratch precursor changing only ID/EX and EX/MEM payload updates measured 73.196 MHz in vendor placement option 1 with 5,202 LUT4 and 1,929 FF, below both champion and acceptance threshold. Its worst path moved to fetch queue payload enables (head_q.instr), which still depended on recovery. This is negative evidence, not a gain. The final proposal includes the explicit IF payload-write separation above; its full three-option timing and correctness gates remain required. The forecast is low confidence.'''\nd['changes'].insert(0,{'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'Separate queue token payload writes from reset/redirect and occupancy updates. Use old occupancy and the new recovery-independent payload_dequeue hint for the exact head/tail write rules in the hypothesis; retain architectural enqueue/dequeue, PC, predictor and occupancy behavior unchanged.'})\nd['changes'].insert(1,{'file':'rtl/hazard_unit.sv','description':'Expose payload_dequeue as decode availability excluding only the redirect kill. Keep decode_accept as payload_dequeue && \"'!redirect and preserve all architectural stall, flush and hold outputs.'\"'})\nfor c in d['changes']:\n if c['file']=='rtl/core.sv':c['description']+=' Wire payload_dequeue from hazard_unit to IF solely for token-payload writes.'\nd['changes'].append({'file':'test/test_if_stage.py','description':'Drive the new payload-only dequeue hint consistently with true decode acceptance and redirects. Preserve all existing fetch/queue/predictor checks. Add exhaustive occupancy/readiness/hold/redirect/reset transition checks proving that only valid tokens are consumed and squashed speculative payload overwrites are unobservable.'})\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()));p.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=90));print('Updated complete hypothesis; schema valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
