{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in ['hyp-20261003-001-r3s0','hyp-20261003-001-r4s0','hyp-20261003-001-r5s0','hyp-20261003-001-r9s0','hyp-20261003-001-r10s0']:\n  print(d['id'],d['title'])\n  print(d.get('hypothesis'));print(d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261003-001-r3s0 Remove redirect from decode payload paths with validity-only flushing\n{'motivation': 'The champion scores 102.93 iterations/s at 46.231 MHz with 4,491,485\\nmeasured CoreMark cycles. Its recorded worst path now runs from the\\nMEM/WB destination register through forwarding, EX branch resolution,\\nIF instruction masking and hazard logic to an ID/EX operand register\\n(27.462 ns reported arrival, 37 cells). Divider retiming has exposed a\\ncontrol path through wide decode data: IF replaces the entire instruction\\nwith a NOP on redirect, and ID clears its entire bundle on flush. Earlier\\nmicro_opt divider experiments improved arithmetic depth but did not\\nproduce the current champion. The strongest new local opportunity is\\nremoving this late redirect signal from decode payload muxes and enables.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"Make pipeline bubbles depend on the existing ID/EX valid bit rather than\\nclearing or masking the whole decode payload. This is a local control\\nfactoring optimization: retain the pipeline stages, branch resolution\\ncycle, forwarding priorities, memory handshake and divider schedule.\\n\\nIn if_stage, drive out.instr directly from imem_data even on flush or\\nredirect. Retain out.valid = !(flush || redirect), the current PC update\\npriorities, and the unchanged imem address interface. Decoding invalid\\nor wrong-path instruction bits is harmless only when validity guards\\nevery downstream consumer with architectural or interlock effects.\\n\\nIn id_stage, separate the ID/EX valid register update from every other\\npayload field. Keep reset initialization. Update pc, instruction, source\\nvalues/addresses, immediate, destination and decoded controls only when\\n!stall; flush must not clear, select, or inhibit these payload updates.\\nUpdate valid with reset/flush priority over stall: clear on reset or\\nflush, hold on stall, otherwise capture in.valid. In particular a\\nload-use bubble clears valid while retaining the stalled old payload;\\na redirect can capture arbitrary raw wrong-path payload with \n…[28031 of 31103 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1c6a0b76636514e1]…\nrefinement remains to be established; the five-percent estimate is speculative. All experiments use scratch RTL outside the repository; only this hypothesis is delivered.', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 5, 'confidence': 'low'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Replace only the branch comparison network with two native 16-bit unsigned comparisons, sign-bit bias selected by branch_op[1], high-half equality, and exact lexicographic merging. Select equality versus ordered relation with branch_op[2], invert with branch_op[0], and retain the explicit reserved-code guard. Preserve all branch/replay/trap/redirect/training controls, forwarded operands and pipeline behavior.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Add focused branch and comparison-immediate coverage at halfword/sign boundaries, including all forwarded operand sources, saved prediction directions, backpressure, replay and alignment traps. Preserve existing progress, latency, flush and RVFI assertions.'}]}\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
