{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_14", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in ['hyp-20261003-001-r7s0','hyp-20261003-001-r8s0','hyp-20261003-002-r8s1','hyp-20261003-002-r10s1']:\n  print(d['id'],d['title']); print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261003-001-r7s0 Flatten EX operand and result muxes with exclusive source enables\nReplace the serial data-selection network around the existing EX\narithmetic with mutually exclusive enables and parallel masked-OR\nselection, at both its operand inputs and final result output.\nThis is one combinational mux-factoring micro-optimization. Preserve\nall pipeline boundaries, instruction latencies,\nissue and retirement width, branch policy, queue and bus handshakes.\n\nFor each source register compute independent EX/MEM and MEM/WB hits\nusing the existing write-control, nonzero destination and address\ncomparisons. Produce three one-hot enables: ex=ex_hit,\nwb=wb_hit&&!ex_hit, and rf=!ex_hit&&!wb_hit. Preserve EX/MEM's younger\nproducer priority. A concrete vector layout is {wb, ex, rf}, replacing\nthe existing two-bit encoding with three source-enable bits throughout\nforward_unit, core and ex_stage. Do not qualify the MEM/WB hit with\nretirement valid: the existing retained WB payload must remain usable\nduring dmem holds after its instruction has retired. Keep x0 excluded\nthrough the nonzero destination checks and existing register-file zero.\n\nForm raw forwarded rs1/rs2 as ORs of the three masked data sources.\nSeparately form alu_a directly from four exclusive sources: PC when\nis_auipc, otherwise the three sources gated by !is_auipc. Likewise\nform alu_b directly from the immediate when alu_src, otherwise the\nthree rs2 sources gated by !alu_src. Do not feed the raw forwarded\nvalue through another PC/immediate data mux. Gate the small