{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_85", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r14s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261003-001-r14s0',\n 'title':'Finish each five-bit divider group with one radix-2 decision',\n 'category':'micro_opt',\n 'motivation':'''The champion scores 182.96 iterations/s at 73.869 MHz and 4,037,538\nCoreMark bracket cycles. The r13s0 timing path crosses div_unit from\nquotient to remainder through 68 cells. Its current recurrence chains\nradix-8 and radix-4 subtraction/selection networks. Earlier local radix\nregrouping improved timing before other changes won those rounds; the\nr10s1 full radix-32 replacement instead grew to 31 parallel trials and\ndid not improve the accepted score. A smaller asymmetric grouping can\nsimplify the final remainder selection without that full expansion.''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Replace only the real divider's combinational five-bit recurrence with\nradix-16 followed by radix-2. Keep the two narrow launch steps, six\nSTEP0..STEP5 cycles, final sign correction and EX/MEM acceptance on\nservice edge eight. Keep native unsigned subtraction operators so Gowin\ncan use its carry resources. This is a local arithmetic micro-optimization,\nwith no new state-machine phase, pipeline stage or execution policy.\n\nAt launch independently form and register unsigned 36-bit odd multiples\nD, 3D, 5D, 7D, 9D, 11D, 13D and 15D from the NEW magnitude_b. Widen\nbefore every shift or addition. Derive even multiples by wiring shifts\nof the appropriate frozen odd multiple. Prefer short constant shift/add\nexpressions; do not cascade one registered multiple into the next or\ninfer a general multiplier. All required multiples remain frozen through\nDONE. Keep original operands and all existing sign/selection flags.\n\nThe first step forms the unsigned 36-bit T16={R,Q[31:28]}. Compute\nfifteen independent 37-bit differences {0,T16}-{0,kD}, k=1..15. Use\neach subtraction's top borrow bit to define fit[k]. Decode exclusive\nenables e[0]=\"'!fit[1], e[k]=fit[k]&&!fit[k+1] for k=1..14, and\ne[15]=fit[15]. Select the low 32 remainder bits and encode digit 0..15\nwith balanced masked-OR trees, avoiding a serial priority mux. Advance\nQ by four bits and append this digit. Preserve full widths until after\nborrow evaluation; for nonzero D the selected remainder is below D.\n\nThe final step forms the 33-bit T2={R_after16,Q_after16[31]}. Perform\none unsigned 34-bit subtraction {0,T2}-{2'\"'b00,D}. If no borrow, select\nthe low 32 difference bits and append quotient bit one; otherwise select\nT2[31:0] and append zero. Register that remainder and updated quotient\nin the existing registers. The final recurrence selection is now a\nsingle two-way mux rather than three fits, four digit enables and a\nfour-way remainder mux. There are sixteen trial subtractors in total,\nversus ten now and thirty-one in the previous full radix-32 proposal.\nThe tradeoff is a wider first-stage selection for a simpler second stage.\n\nUse a 36-bit magnitude for every first-stage multiple because 15D can\nexceed 35 bits. The last subtraction may also be implemented with wider\nzero-extended operands if its original borrow bit remains exact. For\nD=0 all first-stage fits are true and the final fit is true, producing\nall-one quotient digits; retain the existing original-dividend remainder\nand all-one quotient override. Preserve INT_MIN magnitudes, INT_MIN/-1,\nsigned quotient/remainder correction and all four RV32M operations.\n\nKeep the exact RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS expressions and the same control\nschedule; compile real arithmetic out in that mode. Preserve start/busy,\nignored busy starts, captured operands, result_valid, DONE stability\nunder arbitrary backpressure, once-only acceptance and reset cancellation.\nDo not change the standalone combinational ALU, multiplier, forwarding,\nbranch recovery, fetch queue, memory protocol or nret=1 public interface.\nAll decoder, trap, RVFI ordering, liveness and evaluation invariants remain.\n\nValidate against an independent RV32M integer reference and the original\nfive-bit recurrence at each register boundary. Exercise all first-stage\ndigits 0..15 and both final bits, thresholds kD-1/kD/kD+1, unsigned\nhigh-bit operands, signed corners, zero divisors and carry boundaries.\nPreserve every existing timing, hold, arithmetic and progress assertion.\nRun real/ALTOPS divider and pipeline suites, unchanged formal and\nreference-ISS cosimulation, and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/marker checks.\nExpected CoreMark bracket cycles remain exactly 4,037,538 with identical\ninputs and bus stalls.\n\nForecast five percent fitness improvement with low confidence, solely\nthrough Fmax. Acceptance needs more than 191.37616 iterations/s, about\n77.27 MHz at unchanged cycles. Wider first-stage selection, odd-multiple\nsetup, extra routing and competing branch/ALU paths can erase the gain.\nJudge the prescribed median Gowin placement results; neither a shorter\nlast selection network nor one favorable placement establishes a win.\nOnly this hypothesis is delivered; experiments use isolated scratch RTL.''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':5,'confidence':'low'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/div_unit.sv','description':'''Replace radix-8/radix-4 recurrence with exact radix-16/radix-2\ntrial subtraction and balanced exclusive first-digit selection.\nCapture widened odd multiples at launch and simplify the final\nremainder choice to one borrow-controlled mux. Preserve all states,\nlaunch processing, real/ALTOPS semantics, exceptions and handshakes.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_div_unit.py','description':'''Retain the entire suite and add radix-16 digit thresholds, all\nfive-bit recurrence boundary results, wide multiples and signed\ncorner cases against independent integer arithmetic. Check the\nunchanged eight-edge service schedule, live-input changes after\ncapture, ignored busy starts, delayed acceptance and reset cancellation.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Preserve existing pipeline checks and extend DIV/REM dependency\ncases with operands that exercise the new digit thresholds across\nforwarding sources, memory holds and completion backpressure.\nRequire identical RVFI arithmetic, operands, order and progress.'''}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88,default_flow_style=False))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Replaced with schema-valid single divider hypothesis')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
