g,\nbranch recovery, fetch queue, memory protocol or nret=1 public interface.\nAll decoder, trap, RVFI ordering, liveness and evaluation invariants remain.\n\nValidate against an independent RV32M integer reference and the original\nfive-bit recurrence at each register boundary. Exercise all first-stage\ndigits 0..15 and both final bits, thresholds kD-1/kD/kD+1, unsigned\nhigh-bit operands, signed corners, zero divisors and carry boundaries.\nPreserve every existing timing, hold, arithmetic and progress assertion.\nRun real/ALTOPS divider and pipeline suites, unchanged formal and\nreference-ISS cosimulation, and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/marker checks.\nExpected CoreMark bracket cycles remain exactly 4,037,538 with identical\ninputs and bus stalls.\n\nForecast five percent fitness improvement with low confidence, solely\nthrough Fmax. Acceptance needs more than 191.37616 iterations/s, about\n77.27 MHz at unchanged cycles. Wider first-stage selection, odd-multiple\nsetup, extra routing and competing branch/ALU paths can erase the gain.\nJudge the prescribed median Gowin placement results; neither a shorter\nlast selection network nor one favorable placement establishes a win.\nOnly this hypothesis is delivered; experiments use isolated scratch RTL.''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':5,'confidence':'low'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/div_unit.sv','description':'''Replace radix-8/radix-4 recurrence with exact radix-16/radix-2\ntrial subtraction and balanced exclusive first-digit selection.\nCapture widened odd multiples at launch and simplify the final\nremainder choice to one borrow-controlled mux. Preserve all states,\nlaunch processing, real/ALTOPS semantics, exceptions and handshakes.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_div_unit.py','description':'''Retain the entire suite and add radix-16 digit thresholds, all\nfive-bit recurrence boundary results, wide multiples and signed\ncorner cases against independent integer arithmetic. Check the\nunchanged eight-edge service schedule, live-input changes after\ncapture, ignored busy starts, delayed acceptance and reset cancellation.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Preserve existing pipeline checks and extend DIV/REM dependency\ncases with operands that exercise the new digit thresholds across\nforwarding sources, memory holds and completion backpressure.\nRequire identical RVFI arithmetic, operands, order and progress.'''}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88,default_flow_style=False))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Replaced with schema-valid single divider hypothesis')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Replaced with schema-valid single divider hypothesis\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
