},\n    {\n      \"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0\",\n      \"to\": \"dmem_2_dmem_2_0_0_s\",\n      \"slack_ns\": -8.604,\n      \"arrival_ns\": 18.899,\n      \"logic_cells\": 13,\n      \"modules\": [\n        \"clock_ibuf\",\n        \"cpu/u_ex/u_div\",\n        \"cpu/u_ex\",\n        \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\",\n        \"cpu/u_ex\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_90", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema,shutil\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r14s0.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Select divider remainders directly with balanced fit-bit mux trees'\nd['motivation']='''The champion reaches 182.96 iterations/s at 73.869 MHz and 4,037,538\nCoreMark bracket cycles. Recent r13s0 timing exposes a 68-cell divider\nquotient-to-remainder path. The existing radix-8/radix-4 recurrence\ncomputes parallel differences, decodes adjacent fit bits into one-hot\nenables, masks every 32-bit candidate and ORs the words. Earlier full\nradix-32 expansion failed to improve fitness. Keep the successful radix\nand native subtraction mapping, and target only remainder selection.'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Replace the two wide one-hot masked-OR remainder muxes in div_unit\nwith explicitly balanced two-way decision trees driven directly by the\nalready-computed fit bits. Preserve every subtraction, its width and\nborrow interpretation, registered divisor multiple, digit encoder,\nstate transition and service edge. This is one local combinational mux\nmicro-optimization, not a change of divider radix or pipeline structure.\n\nFor the radix-8 result, use exactly this balanced selection topology:\n  r_after8 = fit8[4]\n    ? (fit8[6] ? (fit8[7] ? difference8[7][31:0] : difference8[6][31:0])\n                : (fit8[5] ? difference8[5][31:0] : difference8[4][31:0]))\n    : (fit8[2] ? (fit8[3] ? difference8[3][31:0] : difference8[2][31:0])\n                : (fit8[1] ? difference8[1][31:0] : trial8[31:0]));\nFor the radix-4 result use:\n  r_next = fit4[2]\n    ? (fit4[3] ? difference4[3][31:0] : difference4[2][31:0])\n    : (fit4[1] ? difference4[1][31:0] : trial4[31:0]);\n\nThese are three-level and two-level balanced trees, respectively; do\nnot write descending priority chains. Because the unsigned multiples\nkD are correctly widened, fits are a monotonic thermometer vector:\nfit[k+1] implies fit[k]. Each tree therefore selects precisely the\nlargest fitting digit, including digit zero when no multiple fits.\nFor D=0 every fit is true and each tree selects its largest digit.\nNo approximate comparison or assumption about typical operands is used.\n\nKeep enable8/enable4 and the existing quotient-digit encoding unchanged.\nRemove the now-unused masked8/masked4 declarations and assignments so\nonly the remainder selection topology changes. The intended physical\nbenefit is to bypass adjacent-fit one-hot decoding before wide data\nselection and expose regular mux trees to Gowin's LUT/mux mapping.\nRTL ternaries alone do not guarantee better placement; inspect the\nmapped circuit and judge measured fitness.\n\nRetain the full 36-bit and 35-bit trial subtractions, 35-bit odd\nmultiples, launch magnitude conversion and two narrow initial steps.\nKeep six five-bit recurrence cycles and corrected EX/MEM acceptance\non service edge eight. Preserve original-operand capture, modular\nINT_MIN magnitudes, all DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU signs, INT_MIN/-1, divide-by-zero\nresults, ignored starts while busy, stable DONE under arbitrary holds,\nresult acceptance and reset cancellation. Preserve ALTOPS expressions\nand their control schedule exactly; real arithmetic remains excluded\nunder RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS.\n\nLeave ALU, multiplier, forwarding, predictor, queue, memory handshakes,\nissue/retirement width and all public ports unchanged. Maintain nret=1,\ndecoder legality, traps, RVFI operands and order, memory side-effect\nrules and every correctness/progress assertion. No protected files or\nevaluation assumptions change.\n\nValidate both trees against the existing largest-fit reference for all\nnine radix-8 thermometer patterns and five radix-4 patterns, including\nall-false/all-true. Exercise real recurrence thresholds kD-1/kD/kD+1,\nlarge unsigned multiples, every quotient digit, signed extremes and\nzero divisors. Compare registered quotient/remainder boundaries with\nthe original arithmetic and final results with an independent RV32M\ninteger reference. Retain exact latency and completion-hold tests.\nRun real/ALTOPS divider and pipeline suites, unchanged formal and ISS\ncosimulation, and canonical stalled CoreMark CRC/UART/marker validation.\nExpected bracket cycles are exactly 4,037,538 for identical inputs and\nbus stalls. Full formal remains an implementation-phase requirement.\n\nForecast five percent fitness improvement with low confidence, entirely\nfrom Fmax. Acceptance requires more than 191.37616 iterations/s, about\n77.27 MHz at unchanged cycles. Gowin may refactor both expressions into\nthe same network, mux routing may be slower, or branch/ALU paths may\nlimit the clock. No accepted gain is claimed before complete median\nvendor timing. Only this hypothesis file is delivered; repository RTL\nremains unchanged.'''\nd['changes']=[\n {'file':'rtl/div_unit.sv','description':'''Replace only r_after8 and r_next masked-OR selections with the\nbalanced direct-fit trees specified above; remove dead masked-word\narrays. Preserve native subtractors, widths, fit predicates, quotient\nencoding, divisor setup, states, exceptions and handshake behavior.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_div_unit.py','description':'''Preserve all current arithmetic and timing checks. Add exhaustive\nmonotonic fit-pattern selection equivalence and directed recurrence\nthresholds for every digit, including wide multiples and D=0.\nCheck original recurrence boundaries and independent RV32M results,\nunchanged eight-edge service latency, holds and reset cancellation.'''}]\nclass LiteralDumper(yaml.SafeDumper):pass\ndef represent_str(dumper,data):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',data,style='|' if '\\\\n' in data else None)\nLiteralDumper.add_representer(str,represent_str)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=LiteralDumper,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nroot=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/561ff4c6/8ba1bd50/r14_div_tree');shutil.copytree('cores/bench/test',root/'test',dirs_exist_ok=True)\nprint('Final hypothesis is schema-valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
