{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_33", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r.get('round_id') in (9,10,11) and r.get('category')\"'!='\"'micro_opt':\n  print(r['id'],r['title']);print(r.get('hypothesis',{}).get('hypothesis',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261003-002-r9s1 Precompute conditional-branch recovery before the ID/EX boundary\nPartition conditional-branch resolution into registered static control in ID and dynamic operand comparisons in EX. At the existing ID/EX capture edge, register one-hot controls for the six legal branch predicates, one-hot controls for the predicate that means the captured prediction is wrong, branch-training eligibility derived from direct target alignment, and the single correction destination implied by the captured prediction. This is one structural retiming of the branch-control boundary; it neither adds a pipeline stage nor changes prediction policy, fetch buffering, forwarding selection, ALU/M service schedules or retirement width.\n\nFor a validated branch, form six outcome enables for EQ, NE, signed LT, signed GE, unsigned LT and unsigned GE. For an aligned direct target, form the corresponding six recovery enables after XORing branch_op bit zero with this token's predicted_taken bit. Thus a predicted-not-taken BEQ requests correction on EQ, while a predicted-taken BEQ requests correction on NE; the same complementary pairing applies to signed and unsigned comparisons. All other recovery enables are zero. For a misaligned direct target, actual_taken must be false whether or not the comparison succeeds, so record a separate forced-fallthrough recovery bit equal to predicted_taken. Keep default-illegal decoding unchanged; nonbranches and invalid decode entries must not acquire branch enables.\n\nAlso register two mutually exclusive training classes for legal branches: aligned target, which can train for either outcome, and misaligned target, which may train only if the condition is false. The latter preserves the existing rule that an untaken branch does not fault merely because its encoded target is misaligned. Compute the target alignment from the full-width PC-plus-immediate semantics in ID. Do not truncate architectural targets or wrap addresses. Register one branch_recovery_target alongside this metadata: predicted_take\n…[40717 of 43789 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:73b853212b477d9c]…\nmeasured; acceptance still requires more than 191.37616 iterations/s, approximately 77.27 MHz at the champion's 4037538 bracket cycles, with the clock requirement increasing proportionally if cycles rise.\n\nEvidence and limits: a scratch cache with full instruction equality gating prediction directly in IF validated canonical stalled CoreMark but measured 4044158 bracket cycles and only 69.247/68.725/68.725 MHz across Gowin placements. It is a regression and is not the proposed validation boundary. It shows modest miss overhead but no clock advantage. The final proposal moves a compact immediate/kind identity check to accepted decode and makes the speculative IF target independent of imem_data; that combination has not been built or verified. Do not claim measured improvement from the scratch result. Run unchanged formal and real/ALTOPS unit suites, stalled RVFI cosim, canonical CoreMark validation and all vendor placements on the final implementation; preserve existing liveness and retirement-gap assertions.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\nb=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/561ff4c6/b9a45337/microopt-r15');r=b/'branch_mux';shutil.copytree('cores/bench/rtl',r,dirs_exist_ok=True)\np=r/'ex_stage.sv';s=p.read_text()\nstart=s.index('    case (in.ctrl.branch_op)');end=s.index('    branch_taken',start)\ns=s[:start]+s[end:]\npos=s.index('  always_comb begin\\\\n    branch_taken')\ncode='''  wire [31:0] cmp_source[0:4];\n  assign cmp_source[0]=in.rs1_val;\n  assign cmp_source[1]=in.rs2_val;\n  assign cmp_source[2]=fwd_ex_mem;\n  assign cmp_source[3]=fwd_wb_alu;\n  assign cmp_source[4]=fwd_wb_load;\n  wire eq_pair[0:4][0:4];\n  wire lt_pair[0:4][0:4];\n  generate for(genvar x=0;x<5;x=x+1) begin:g_cx\n    for(genvar y=0;y<5;y=y+1) begin:g_cy\n      if(x==y) begin:g_same\n        assign eq_pair[x][y]=1'b1;\n        assign lt_pair[x][y]=1'b0;\n      end else if(x<y) begin:g_cmp\n        assign eq_pair[x][y]=cmp_source[x]==cmp_source[y];\n        assign lt_pair[x][y]=cmp_source[x]<cmp_source[y];\n      end else begin:g_reverse\n        assign eq_pair[x][y]=eq_pair[y][x];\n        assign lt_pair[x][y]=\"'!eq_pair[y][x]&&!lt_pair[y][x];\n      end\n    end\n  end endgenerate\n  wire [15:0] condition_lane;\n  generate for(genvar i=0;i<4;i=i+1) begin:g_left\n    for(genvar j=0;j<4;j=j+1) begin:g_right\n      localparam integer X=i==0?0:i+1;\n      localparam integer Y=j==0?1:j+1;\n      wire slt=(cmp_source[X][31]''^cmp_source[Y][31])?cmp_source[X][31]:lt_pair[X][Y];\n      logic cond;\n      always_comb begin\n        case(in.ctrl.branch_op)\n          BR_BEQ: cond=eq_pair[X][Y];\n          BR_BNE: cond=!eq_pair[X][Y];\n          BR_BLT: cond=slt;\n          BR_BGE: cond=!slt;\n          BR_BLTU:cond=lt_pair[X][Y];\n          BR_BGEU:cond=!lt_pair[X][Y];\n          default:cond=1'\"'b0;\n        endcase\n      end\n      assign condition_lane[i*4+j]=fwd_rs1_sel[i]&&fwd_rs