{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_60", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r15s0.yaml')\np.write_text('''id: hyp-20261003-001-r15s0\ntitle: \\\"Register complete ALU source choices before execute\\\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The successful r7s1 and r8s2 changes moved forwarding decisions before\n  EX, but the champion still combines each registered forwarding bit\n  with \"'!is_auipc or !alu_src inside EX. Those gates feed wide operand\n  muxes, and the same raw forwarding controls also drive branch and\n  M-unit operand selection. Recent recovery and divider-mux experiments\n  left the ordinary ALU/address cone critical. Completing operand-source\n  selection at the existing ID/EX edge can remove that remaining control\n  layer and separate raw-source fanout from ALU-source fanout.\nhypothesis: |\n  Register the complete five-way ALU source enables alongside the existing\n  four-way raw forwarding enables. This is one local operand-mux control\n  optimization. Preserve the pipeline, instruction latencies, predictor,\n  fetch queue, ALU arithmetic and M-unit schedules. Do not add an operand\n  data register or a new stage, change the source prediction policy, or\n  weaken canceled-write verification.\n\n  Export the selected ID token'\"'s positively decoded is_auipc and alu_src\n  from id_stage to forward_unit through internal core wiring. Use the\n  actual decoder outputs, including their existing illegal-instruction\n  behavior; do not infer them from an incomplete opcode shortcut. Form\n  the existing next raw mask F={WB_load,WB_ALU,EX_MEM,RF} with precisely\n  the current dependency comparisons, youngest-writer priority, x0\n  exclusion and MEM permission qualification. On the same ID/EX edge,\n  independently capture A={is_auipc, F1 & {4{\"'!is_auipc}}} and\n  B={alu_src, F2 & {4{!alu_src}}}. Bits 0..3 retain the current source\n  encoding; bit 4 selects this instruction'\"'s PC for A or immediate for B.\n  Keep the original raw masks unchanged for branches, JALR, stores,\n  multiplier/divider launches, RVFI operands and permission verification.\n\n  The new masks must have exactly the original mask-register priorities:\n  reset or flush clears all bits; a dmem hold retains them; an invalid\n  ordinary capture clears them; valid decode captures the new five-way\n  choices. During stall_id && \"'!stall_ex_mem, apply the existing M-wait\n  source aging to bits 0..3 if bit 4 is clear: an EX/MEM source becomes\n  WB-load or WB-ALU according to ex_mem_load, and all other raw choices\n  become RF, exactly as the existing raw-mask update does. If bit 4 is\n  set, retain the override-only mask. Never derive a held instruction'\"'s\n  override from the changing live decode token. Flush retains priority\n  over a load-use stall. Captured M operands and retained WB data continue\n  to supply their existing consumers exactly as before.\n\n  In EX compute alu_a and alu_b directly as balanced ORs of five masked\n  words driven only by these registered enables. Remove is_auipc/alu_src\n  qualification from each ALU forwarding lane and drive the PC/immediate\n  lanes from bit 4. Do not recreate a raw-rs then PC/immediate serial mux.\n  Keep the original raw rs1/rs2 forwarding muxes and all their consumers.\n  An override suppresses an ALU operand only; it must not suppress the\n  original raw-source permission check or change the existing replay\n  behavior for incidental instruction-field matches.\n\n  The intended invariant is that, for each valid held or advancing token,\n  new_A equals {in.ctrl.is_auipc, raw_F1 & {4{\"'!in.ctrl.is_auipc}}}, and\n  new_B equals {in.ctrl.alu_src, raw_F2 & {4{!in.ctrl.alu_src}}}.\n  Both masks are zero on a freshly cleared bubble, and each valid mask\n  is one-hot. Verify these properties from reachable reset and pipeline\n  transitions without adding formal assumptions. They establish identical\n  ALU operands while moving the small override gates before the register.\n  The new registers carry genuinely different control from the raw masks;\n  do not rely on preservation attributes or artificial physical constraints.\n\n  Preserve nret=1 and all external ports, decoder default-illegal rules,\n  exact traps, full-width addresses, RVFI operands/next-PC/order, memory\n  side-effect suppression and all existing progress bounds. Keep ALTOPS\n  formulas, real arithmetic, eight-edge division and two-edge multiply\n  unchanged. No evaluation, wrapper, constraint or benchmark files change.\n\n  Expect exactly 4,037,538 canonical CoreMark bracket cycles for identical\n  inputs and bus stalls. Forecast 6% higher fitness with low confidence,\n  entirely from Fmax; acceptance requires more than 191.37616 iterations/s,\n  approximately 77.27 MHz at that cycle count. Added ID decode fanout,\n  extra mask flops and unchanged branch/divider paths may cap the gain.\n  Judge the prescribed three-placement Gowin median and actual CoreMark\n  cycles; this forecast is not a measured acceptance result.\n\n  Preserve every existing pipeline assertion. Add checks of both mask\n  invariants and exact operand equivalence through every source choice,\n  simultaneous producer matches, PC/immediate substitutions, x0,\n  load-use bubbles, independent long bus holds, M launch/wait/completion,\n  reset, branch flush and canceled-write replay. Include AUIPC, LUI,\n  immediate arithmetic, loads/stores and JALR with coincidental source\n  matches. Run real/ALTOPS pipeline and ALU suites, unchanged formal,\n  reference-ISS cosimulation and canonical stalled CoreMark CRC/UART,\n  bounds and timing-marker validation.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Expose the selected token'\"'s existing decoded is_auipc and alu_src as\n      internal outputs. Preserve decoder logic and ID/EX payload/control\n      capture, flush, invalid-bubble and hold behavior.\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Capture separate five-way ALU-A and ALU-B source enables on the same\n      edge as the unchanged raw forwarding masks. Fold decoded overrides\n      into these new masks before capture and implement exact reset,\n      flush, invalid, dmem-hold and M-wait-aging behavior. Keep the original\n      raw prediction and permission-failure equations unchanged.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Wire decoded override flags from ID into the forwarding controller\n      and the two five-bit registered masks into EX. Preserve existing\n      raw source masks, replay wiring and all public IO/RVFI ports.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Drive the five ALU operand lanes directly from registered complete\n      source enables, removing post-register override qualification.\n      Retain the raw forwarding muxes, arithmetic, branch resolution,\n      M launches/snapshots, write-permission replay and register updates.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Add independent checks that complete masks produce the original\n      operands for every valid token and retain exact override/source\n      coherence through holds, bubbles, flushes and M waits. Cover all\n      forwarding sources, source collisions, x0 and canceled producers.\n      Preserve all ISA, RVFI, memory, exact-latency and progress assertions.\n''')\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text());jsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Revised hypothesis is schema-valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
