 and 199.837 ns arrival\\ntime. The ALU describes signed and unsigned division and remainder with\\nseparate / and % expressions. Their combinational implementation is the\\nstrongest suspected source of the very deep arithmetic path, even when\\nCoreMark executes few divisions. The history contains only the baseline\\nand there is no LESSONS.md or previous divider optimization to reuse.\\n\", \"hypothesi\n…[68828 of 71900 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:381b16ad6ffbb141]…\n, \"vs_baseline\": 1075.91, \"fmax_mhz\": 57.541, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4037538, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3979, \"ff\": 989, \"seeds\": [53.956, 57.541, 57.541], \"perturbations\": [[0, 53.956, 16], [1, 57.541, 16], [2, 57.541, 16]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -13.534, \"arrival_ns\": 23.828, \"logic_cells\": 16, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 16, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T08:20:34.800803Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 6, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-002-r6s1 (improvement, +18.24%): Combining registered 17-by-17 multiplier partials with radix-8/radix-4 division and registered odd multiples removes both M-extension timing bottlenecks while preserving a shallow two-trial divider launch, so clock gains outweigh CoreMark's small extra multiplier-stall cost.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
