changes alone measured only\n  a 0.91 percent median Fmax gain; the proposed complete EX selection\n  rewrite measured a 7.53 percent fitness gain in the scratch prototype.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the serial data-selection network around the existing EX\n  arithmetic with mutually exclusive enables and parallel masked-OR\n  selection, at both its operand inputs and final result output.\n  This is one combinational mux-factoring micro-optimization. Preserve\n  all pipeline boundaries, instruction latencies,\n  issue and retirement width, branch policy, queue and bus handshakes.\n\n  For each source register compute independent EX/MEM and MEM/WB hits\n  using the existing write-control, nonzero destination and address\n  comparisons. Produce three one-hot enables: ex=ex_hit,\n  wb=wb_hit&&!ex_hit, and rf=!ex_hit&&!wb_hit. Preserve EX/MEM's younger\n  producer prior\n…[5427 of 8499 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9588e95d494decf7]…\nn and RVFI behavior unchanged.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Use parallel masked-OR forwarding for raw source operands, and\n      directly select ALU operands from exclusive register/bypass/PC or\n      immediate sources. Remove the serial raw-forwarding-to-ALU-mux\n      dependency. Replace the nested EX/MEM result ternary with the four\n      exclusive masked DIV/MUL/link/fast-ALU words specified above.\n      Preserve branch, store, M-unit and RVFI uses of the original\n      post-forward register operands, the ALU's internal implementation,\n      and every register update, hold and acceptance rule.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve all existing checks and add directed producer-priority,\n      x0, PC/immediate-override and held-WB forwarding cases for both\n      source ports. Cover ALU, branch/JALR, memory and M consumers under\n      bus stalls, checking exact RVFI operands/results/order and\n      once-only memory effects without relaxing latency asserti