{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_78", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r8s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261003-001-r8s0\ntitle: \"Shorten integer ADD and SUB with parallel block carry selection\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 173.56 iterations/s at 70.074 MHz and 4,037,538\n  CoreMark bracket cycles. Its recorded worst path now starts at an\n  EX/MEM write-control register and crosses operand forwarding and the\n  ordinary ALU before reaching data-memory BSRAM, with 21.0 ns arrival.\n  The successful register-file and forwarding retiming removed earlier\n  operand-delivery limits, making the combinational integer arithmetic\n  a useful next target. Prior mux flattening alone gained only 2.47\n  percent; the proposal attacks carry propagation inside the ALU instead.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the ordinary ALU's full-width ADD and SUB expressions with\n  parallel eight-bit block arithmetic and explicit group carry lookahead.\n  Preserve its combinational interface, operation encodings, every\n  pipeline register and the complete instruction/cycle schedule. This\n  is one local arithmetic micro-optimization, with no new execution\n  stage, speculation, memory mechanism or change to M-unit schedules.\n\n  Implement a reusable 32-bit combinational sum function taking unsigned\n  x, y and carry-in. In each of four eight-bit blocks compute the\n  nine-bit zero-carry sum independently. Its high bit is block generate;\n  block propagate is the reduction AND of x XOR y over that block.\n  Compute carries into blocks 1, 2 and 3 directly from block generate,\n  propagate and initial carry, rather than rippling through selected\n  block results. In parallel compute each block's candidate low sum\n  for carry-in zero and one, then select with its looked-ahead carry.\n  Express carry-one candidates as independent small additions, avoiding\n  a full-width incrementer after the zero-carry sum. All arithmetic must\n  have explicit unsigned widths and return the sum modulo 2^32.\n\n  Use this circuit for ADD(x=a,y=b,cin=0) and independently for\n  SUB(x=a,y=~b,cin=1). Keep ADD free of an opcode-controlled conditional\n  inversion o\n…[1038 of 4110 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2139d8c697fd3daa]…\n\n  increase area/routing, and Gowin may already optimize the original\n  addition or move the limit to another path. Inspect mapped vendor\n  timing and score the median across placement options. This initial\n  forecast is not a measured candidate result.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Implement an explicitly unsigned four-block carry-lookahead and\n      carry-select sum function. Use separate instances for ordinary\n      ADD and SUB, leaving ADD's operand path free of subtraction-mode\n      inversion. Preserve the combinational interface, all other\n      operations, M generate parameters and ALTOPS substitutions.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve every existing test and add directed and fixed-seed\n      randomized ADD/SUB checks against modular integer references.\n      Stress generate/propagate transitions and carry/borrow across\n      bits 8, 16 and 24, zero/all-ones, INT_MIN/INT_MAX and overflow.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
