{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"agent_message","text":"The timing trials keep exposing another EX-to-memory or divider path after each local reduction. I’m testing one broader result-selection change: decode one-hot operation selects before ID/EX, then select directly from arithmetic, link, multiply and divide results at EX/MEM. This removes the late ALU decode and nested result mux without changing instruction latency."}}
