med until the prototype or implementation passes the unchanged checks and median Gowin timing. Acceptance requires actual fitness above 191.37616 iterations/s, using the measured bracket cycle count rather than assuming every old multiply hold disappears.\n\nValidate independent back-to-back multiplies, all signed/high-half variants, same-edge old-result acceptance and new launch, dependency chains into ALU/branch/load/store/MUL/DIV, multiple writers to the same register, x0, held older memory operations, simultaneous bus stalls, reset and canceled-source replay. Preserve the standalone arithmetic tests and add explicit pipelined-mode handshake tests. Run all existing real/ALTOPS pipeline and arithmetic checks, unchanged formal and stalled RVFI cosimulation, and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/marker/bounds validation. Preserve all existing progress bounds, nret=1 and external ports. This is one retiming of multiplication across existing stages; do not change predictor policy, divider recurrence, memory protocol or evaluation files.''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':7,'confidence':'low'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/mul_unit.sv','description':'Add a default-off pipelined handshake mode that accepts a new launch simultaneously with acceptance of the old registered partial products. Preserve existing blocking mode, exact real/ALTOPS arithmetic, signed limb widths, result stability and reset cancellation. All current standalone assertions remain valid in default mode.'},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Launch multiplication on the ordinary EX advance, recording current validated forwarded operands in EX/MEM. Remove MUL from execute_wait and from the blocking-unit replay exemption. Remove multiply completion from EX/MEM.alu_result selection; mark its result kind for MEM/WB read_data. Expose the registered-partial completion to MEM and take acceptance from the older MEM token. Keep blocking division, replay, branch and trap behavior unchanged.'},\n {'f