{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_56","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r11s1.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']=5\nd['hypothesis']=d['hypothesis'].replace('Forecast seven percent higher fitness','Forecast five percent higher fitness').replace('The seven-percent forecast requires further physical improvement and remains low confidence.','The five-percent forecast remains low confidence; it additionally relies on eliminating redundant multiplier-local dispatch gating as specified below, which was not measured in this prototype.')\nd['hypothesis']+='''\\\\n\\\\nFinal structural refinement: in the core's pipelined multiplier mode, make the existing EX/MEM token the sole owner of multiplier capacity. Define multiply launch directly from the valid legal advancing EX token, older-memory hold and verified operands, without serializing its partial-product capture enable through mul_busy/result_valid or a redundant local pending-state mux. At every launch the previous partials are either unused or simultaneously accepted by the older MEM multiply; prove this invariant from stage movement, with no new formal assumptions. The core must never assert launch while an older multiply result is unaccepted. In pipelined mode, start therefore directly captures all partials and metadata; any pending flag retained for observability mirrors ownership but does not gate their data capture. Keep the default standalone blocking mode's existing busy-start rejection unchanged. Keep EX/MEM hold and MEM acceptance priorities intact, including reset. This removes the unnecessary second capacity controller rather than merely increasing its readiness logic. The measured prototype still retained that redundant local/core busy qualification; the refined final control has not been timed or fully verified. It is the concrete additional clock-improvement hypothesis, and may still fail the acceptance margin.\\\\n\\\\nA unified registered WB-value scratch variant regressed to 70.240 MHz median; it is excluded. Keep the current separate registered ALU/load result banks and four-source forwarding topology. Deliver only this YAML, leaving repository RTL unchanged.'''\nfor c in d['changes']:\n if c['file']=='rtl/mul_unit.sv':\n  c['description']+=' In core pipelined mode use start directly as partial-product capture enable, with EX/MEM owning capacity; remove redundant pending qualification from that mode. Prove the core never launches over an unaccepted result; retain legacy rejection in default blocking mode.'\n if c['file']=='rtl/ex_stage.sv':\n  c['description']+=' Derive pipelined multiply start directly from legal advancing verified EX work; do not put multiplier-local busy in this enable, since EX/MEM already owns capacity.'\n if c['file']=='test/test_pipeline.py':\n  c['description']+=' Assert on every multiplier launch that any older pending product is simultaneously accepted, including all memory holds and reset, without adding formal assumptions.'\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef represent_string(dumper,value):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',value,style='|' if '\\\\n' in value else None)\nDumper.add_representer(str,represent_string)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert d['id']=='hyp-20261003-002-r11s1' and d['category']=='structural'\nassert -50 <= d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct'] <= 50\nprint('Final hypothesis:',p)\nprint('Category:',d['category'],'Forecast:',d['expected_impact'])\nprint('Bytes:',p.stat().st_size)\nPY\ngit status --short\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
