{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_29", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id'].endswith(('r4s0','r5s0')):\n  h=d['hypothesis']; print(d['id'],h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261003-001-r4s0 Replace only the real divider's five serial radix-2 steps per STEP0\nthrough STEP5 cycle with two radix-4 restoring steps followed by one\nradix-2 restoring step. Each cycle still consumes exactly five dividend\nbits. Keep the current launch edge's two narrow steps, six recurrence\nedges, and final corrected EX/MEM acceptance edge. This is a local\ncombinational arithmetic replacement with unchanged interface, state\nschedule, instruction latency, pipeline, predictor and bus handshakes.\nThe mechanism is five dependent subtract/select boundaries becoming\nthree, with the three candidate subtractions of each radix-4 step\nevaluated in parallel.\n\nAt launch compute unsigned dividend and divisor magnitudes exactly as\ntoday. Retain the current quotient/remainder initialization after the\ntop two dividend bits. Also register 3D from the new divisor magnitude,\nusing explicitly widened 34-bit operands before shifting or adding.\nD is the registered 32-bit divisor; form 34-bit D and 2D by zero\nextension and wiring, and hold the registered 34-bit 3D for the entire\noperation. Do not derive 3D from the previous divisor register, compute\nit on the recurrence path, or add a preparation cycle. The launch\nmagnitude-to-3D adder is a timing risk to check in Gowin.\n\nFor each radix-4 step form unsigned T={R[31:0],Q[31:30]} at 34 bits.\nIn parallel compute 35-bit differences {1'b0,T}-{1'b0,D34},\n{1'b0,T}-{1'b0,D2_34}, and {1'b0,T}-{1'b0,D3_34}. Each high bit is\nan unsigned borrow. Choose digit 3 when 3D fits, else digit 2 when\n2D fits, else digit 1 when D fits, otherwise digit 0. Express exclusive\ndigit enables and a parallel masked-OR result selection so a priority\ncascade of wide muxes does not replace the removed arithmetic depth.\nThe next remainder is the selected difference's low 32 bits, or\nT[31:0] for digit 0; shift Q left two bits and append the selected\ntwo-bit digit. For nonzero D, R<D proves the chosen remainder fits\n32 bits even when the unselected trial or multiples do not.\n\nAfter two such steps, apply one exis\n…[7026 of 10098 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2c78391fd0f61b39]…\n validation text,\ncompletion, in-bounds accesses and timing markers, reporting exactly\n4,010,178 bracket cycles for ten iterations with both stall streams.\nTheir product is 128.94191 iterations/s, 6.9791 percent above 120.53.\nThis is prototype evidence, not an official tournament acceptance.\n\nAll three existing divider cocotb tests passed in both real and\nALTOPS builds, including exact service latency, delayed acceptance\nand reset cancellation. Selftest and all three random RVFI programs\npassed the unchanged ISS comparison both with and without bus stalls.\nA width-accurate numerical model additionally matched 69,572 RV32M\nresults over 17,393 operand pairs and the original radix-2 recurrence\nat 208,716 group boundaries; it exercised all radix-8 and radix-4\ndigits and checked nonzero-divisor remainder bounds. Formal proofs\nwere not rerun for this proposal and remain required implementation\ngates. Only the hypothesis file is delivered; the prototype and its\nbuild artifacts were kept outside the repository RTL.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"mkdir -p /srv/hwebench/tmp/561ff4c6/89854cc9/hyp-r12-branch/rtl\npython - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\np=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/561ff4c6/89854cc9/hyp-r12-branch/rtl')\nfor f in Path('cores/bench/rtl').glob('*.sv'):shutil.copy(f,p/f.name)\nf=p/'ex_stage.sv';s=f.read_text();a=s.index('    case (in.ctrl.branch_op)');b=s.index('    branch_taken  =',a)\ns=s[:a]+s[b:]\na=s.index('  always_comb begin\\\\n    branch_taken  =')\ns=s[:a]+'''  wire [31:0] br_a [0:3];\n  wire [31:0] br_b [0:3];\n  wire [15:0] br_masked;\n  assign br_a[0]=in.rs1_val;\n  assign br_b[0]=in.rs2_val;\n  assign br_a[1]=fwd_ex_mem;\n  assign br_b[1]=fwd_ex_mem;\n  assign br_a[2]=fwd_wb_alu;\n  assign br_b[2]=fwd_wb_alu;\n  assign br_a[3]=fwd_wb_load;\n  assign br_b[3]=fwd_wb_load;\n  generate for(genvar ai=0;ai<4;ai++) begin : g_br_a\n    for(genvar bi=0;bi<4;bi++) begin : g_br_b\n      logic cond;\n      always_comb begin\n        case (in.ctrl.branch_op)\n          BR_BEQ: cond = br_a[ai] == br_b[bi];\n          BR_BNE: cond = br_a[ai] \"'!= br_b[bi];\n          BR_BLT: cond = $signed(br_a[ai]) < $signed(br_b[bi]);\n          BR_BGE: cond = $signed(br_a[ai]) >= $signed(br_b[bi]);\n          BR_BLTU: cond = br_a[ai] < br_b[bi];\n          BR_BGEU: cond = br_a[ai] >= br_b[bi];\n          default: cond = 1'\"'b0;\n        endcase\n      end\n      assign br_masked[4*ai+bi]=cond && fwd_rs1_sel[ai] && fwd_rs2_sel[bi];\n    end\n  end endgenerate\n  assign branch_cond = |br_masked;\n'''+s[a:];f.write_text(s)\nPY\npython - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom tools.eval.gowin import build_all, summarize\nimport json\np=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/561ff4c6/89854cc9/hyp-r12-branch')\nr=build_all(Path.cwd(),p/'rtl','fpga/core_bench_si.sv',p/'timing')\n(p/'timing.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2));print(json.dumps(summarize(r)))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
