{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/561ff4c6/89854cc9/hyp-r12-rf/rtl/reg_file.sv');s=p.read_text()\na=s.index('  assign rs1_data =');s=s[:a]+'''  wire en10 = \"'!bypass1 && valid_bits[rs1_addr] && !rs1_addr[4];\n  wire en11 = !bypass1 && valid_bits[rs1_addr] && rs1_addr[4];\n  wire en20 = !bypass2 && valid_bits[rs2_addr] && !rs2_addr[4];\n  wire en21 = !bypass2 && valid_bits[rs2_addr] && rs2_addr[4];\n  assign rs1_data = (read1[0] & {32{en10}}) | (read1[1] & {32{en11}}) | (w_data & {32{bypass1}});\n  assign rs2_data = (read2[0] & {32{en20}}) | (read2[1] & {32{en21}}) | (w_data & {32{bypass2}});\nendmodule\n'\"''';p.write_text(s)\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r12s1.yaml');s=p.read_text();s=s.replace('  Mask invalid data with a conditional selection that guarantees a\\\\n  defined zero; never expose an uninitialized RAM word through RVFI.','''  Implement the final read selection as three mutually exclusive lanes:\n  bank0 enabled by \"'!bypass && valid[rs] && !rs[4], bank1 enabled by\n  !bypass && valid[rs] && rs[4], and w_data enabled by bypass. Combine\n  the enabled words in a balanced parallel OR; do not cascade a bank\n  mux, a zero-validity mux and a final WB mux on the 32-bit data path.\n  Qualify each bank word with a conditional expression that returns\n  literal zero when disabled, rather than X & 0 masking, so uninitialized\n  payload never leaks during four-state simulation. The bypass wins\n  without depending on the stored valid bit.'\"''')\ns=s.replace('  measured score. Judge the complete vendor placement median and actual','  measured winning score. Judge the complete vendor placement median and actual')\ns=s.replace('changes:\\\\n','''changes:\n''',1)\ns=s.replace('      Preserve the module interface and ID/EX read-capture latency. Check','''      Fold bank selection, valid masking and WB bypass into one parallel\n      three-lane output selection as specified above; avoid serial muxes.\n      Preserve the module interface and ID/EX read-capture latency. Check''')\nneedle='expected_impact:\\\\n'\nevidence='''  Prototype evidence: the replicated-RAM storage with a serial bank,\n  validity and bypass output selection passed the unchanged canonical\n  CoreMark validator at exactly 4,037,538 cycles, no out-of-bounds access\n  and all expected CRCs. It mapped to 4,180 LUT4, 968 registers, 32 RAM16\n  resources, four BSRAMs and two DSPs. Its placement frequencies were\n  66.848/68.209/68.209 MHz, a regression. That prototype is not evidence\n  of a fitness gain. The final proposal additionally flattens the output\n  selection as described above; its timing and full formal validation\n  remain unestablished. The six-percent forecast is low confidence and\n  requires a substantial clock recovery, not just the proven area saving.\n  Deliver only this hypothesis; repository RTL remains unchanged.\n'''\ns=s.replace(needle,evidence+needle);p.write_text(s)\nPY\npython - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom tools.eval.gowin import build_all,summarize\nimport json\np=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/561ff4c6/89854cc9/hyp-r12-rf')\nr=build_all(Path.cwd(),p/'rtl','fpga/core_bench_si.sv',p/'timing_parallel')\n(p/'timing_parallel.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2));print(json.dumps(summarize(r)))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
