{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nwanted={'hyp-20261003-002-r8s1','hyp-20261003-002-r9s1','hyp-20261003-002-r10s1','hyp-20261003-003-r7s2'}\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in wanted:\n  h=d['hypothesis']; print('\\\\n',d['id'],d['title']); print(h['hypothesis'] if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\nrg --files cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses cores/bench/test | head -60\"", "aggregated_output": "\n hyp-20261003-003-r7s2 Register branch prediction recovery outside the execute feedback path\nRegister all branch-prediction corrections alongside the resolving\ninstruction's EX/MEM entry. Use that older registered correction to\nredirect fetch and squash the younger EX instruction on the following\ncycle. Keep the current direction predictor, immediate-derived direct\ntargets, fetch queue, load-use interlocks and M-extension units. This\nis one predictor recovery mechanism: trade an extra recovery cycle on\na miss for a shorter operand-comparison-to-global-control path.\n\nIn EX, retain the existing full-width target arithmetic, forwarded\ncomparison, target alignment checks and architectural next-PC rules.\nWhen a valid instruction advances, capture a mismatch bit comparing\nactual_taken with its saved predicted_taken, and capture the actual\nsuccessor as the correction target. JALR remains predicted not taken.\nDo not drive fetch, ID flush or ordinary branch training from that\ncycle's raw EX mismatch. Correctly predicted instructions continue at\nunchanged throughput; only a mismatch adds one recovery cycle.\n\nThe correction becomes visible from the registered resolving token in\nMEM. Before the younger EX token can enter EX/MEM, it discards that\nyounger token, clears ID/EX validity and live side-effect controls,\nempties the fetch\nqueue and resets ID/EX validity, while sending the registered actual\nsuccessor to fetch. It must override a younger load-use indication,\nexecute_wait, branch result, M-unit start and result acceptance, and\nan unready instruction bus. A wrong-path store or load has not yet\nreached MEM and must never issue a request. A younger multiply/divide\nmust be prevented from launching on the correction cycle; do not let\nits wait signal block correction. No architectural rollback is needed.\n\nService a pending correction for exactly one cycle while retaining\nits resolving instruction in EX/MEM. On that edge, clear only its\ncorrection-pending bit, issue the redirect, kill the younger EX/ID\nwork, and insert a WB b\n…[20273 of 23345 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7aab60b064fde8cc]…\neration with a special first recurrence were\nslower. A carry-save odd-multiple setup also regressed to 71.608 MHz\nmedian and 7,617 LUT4, exposing a launch path; prefer independent\nordinary shift/add/subtract expressions with few terms for each odd\nmultiple. Likewise, separate scratch validity/payload and speculative\nbranch-comparison changes regressed and are excluded from this proposal.\nThe six percent forecast is low-confidence and requires further benefit\nfrom the implemented physical arithmetic layout beyond the measured\nprototype; do not report the current prototype as an accepted gain.\nDeliver only this hypothesis, leaving repository RTL unchanged.\n\ncores/bench/test/test_mul_unit.py\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py\ncores/bench/test/test_if_stage.py\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py\ncores/bench/test/test_hazard_unit.py\ncores/bench/test/test_div_unit.py\ncores/bench/test/conftest.py\ncores/bench/test/test_imm_gen.py\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
