{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_12", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in ['hyp-20261003-002-r9s1','hyp-20261003-002-r10s1','hyp-20261003-001-r10s0']:\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print(d['id'],d['title'],d['outcome'],d.get('fmax_mhz'),d.get('critical_path'))\n  print(h.get('hypothesis',h) if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print(d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261003-002-r9s1 Precompute conditional-branch recovery before the ID/EX boundary regression 70.837 {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.read_data_0_s0', 'to': 'dmem_3_dmem_3_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -11.706, 'arrival_ns': 22.0, 'logic_cells': 13, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nPartition conditional-branch resolution into registered static control in ID and dynamic operand comparisons in EX. At the existing ID/EX capture edge, register one-hot controls for the six legal branch predicates, one-hot controls for the predicate that means the captured prediction is wrong, branch-training eligibility derived from direct target alignment, and the single correction destination implied by the captured prediction. This is one structural retiming of the branch-control boundary; it neither adds a pipeline stage nor changes prediction policy, fetch buffering, forwarding selection, ALU/M service schedules or retirement width.\n\nFor a validated branch, form six outcome enables for EQ, NE, signed LT, signed GE, unsigned LT and unsigned GE. For an aligned direct target, form the corresponding six recovery enables after XORing branch_op bit zero with this token's predicted_taken bit. Thus a predicted-not-taken BEQ requests correction on EQ, while a predicted-taken BEQ requests correction on NE; the same complementary pairing applies to signed and unsigned comparisons. All other recovery enables are zero. For a misaligned direct target, actual_taken must be false whether or not the comparison succeeds, so record a separate forced-fallthrough recovery bit equal to predicted_taken. Keep default-illegal decoding unchanged; nonbranches and invalid decode entries must not acquire branch enables.\n\nAlso register two mutually exclusive training classes for legal branches: aligned target, which can train for either outcome, and misaligned target, which may train only if the condition is false. The latter preserves the existing rule that an untaken branch does not fault merely because its encoded target is misaligne\n…[14800 of 17872 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:783d21db4ea1fdd5]…\ns\nstalls. Full implementation-phase formal and timing gates remain\nrequired. The ALTOPS arithmetic and state schedule are unchanged.\n\nKeep the launch-generated, frozen multiples and parallel remainder\ndifferences in the final design. Scratch variants that select a\nmultiple before a shared remainder subtraction, remove multiple reset,\nor overlap multiple generation with a special first recurrence were\nslower. A carry-save odd-multiple setup also regressed to 71.608 MHz\nmedian and 7,617 LUT4, exposing a launch path; prefer independent\nordinary shift/add/subtract expressions with few terms for each odd\nmultiple. Likewise, separate scratch validity/payload and speculative\nbranch-comparison changes regressed and are excluded from this proposal.\nThe six percent forecast is low-confidence and requires further benefit\nfrom the implemented physical arithmetic layout beyond the measured\nprototype; do not report the current prototype as an accepted gain.\nDeliver only this hypothesis, leaving repository RTL unchanged.\n\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
