{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n s=h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else str(h)\n if any(x in s.lower() for x in ['pairwise','source pair','all source','parallel branch','speculative branch','elastic','six-stage','operand stage']):\n  print(d['id'],d['title'])\n  for p in s.split('\\\\n\\\\n'):\n   if any(x in p.lower() for x in ['pairwise','source pair','all source','parallel branch','speculative branch','elastic','six-stage','operand stage']): print(p)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20261003-001-r7s0 Flatten EX operand and result muxes with exclusive source enables\nForm raw forwarded rs1/rs2 as ORs of the three masked data sources.\nSeparately form alu_a directly from four exclusive sources: PC when\nis_auipc, otherwise the three sources gated by !is_auipc. Likewise\nform alu_b directly from the immediate when alu_src, otherwise the\nthree rs2 sources gated by !alu_src. Do not feed the raw forwarded\nvalue through another PC/immediate data mux. Gate the small source\nenables before the wide data selection, and express balanced ORs of\nmasked words so the intended hardware has no wide priority cascade.\nRaw forwarded values still feed branch comparisons, JALR, stores,\nM-unit launch and captured RVFI operands; immediate and PC overrides\naffect only ALU operands. Keep the existing alu.sv arithmetic and its\ninternal case selection, both M units and register-file mapping.\nhyp-20261003-003-r10s2 Speculate narrow ordered-branch verification with selective correction\nAdd one static operand-width predictor for BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU verification. Speculate that rs1[31:8] equals rs2[31:8], so unsigned rs1[7:0] < rs2[7:0] predicts less-than for both signed and unsigned ordered branches. Apply funct3 bit-zero inversion for BGE/BGEU. Use this speculative branch condition, legal instruction qualification and direct-target alignment to perform the existing same-cycle comparison against the saved fetch predicted_taken bit. Correct fetch immediately if the narrow condition disagrees with that bit. BEQ/BNE retain exact equality verification; JAL/JALR retain their existing behavior. Keep the fetch table, instruction-derived direct targets and queue unchanged.\nhyp-20261003-002-r13s1 Absorb fetch stalls with an eight-entry instruction queue\nThis is solely a structural increase in elastic fetch capacity. Preserve\nall EX/MEM/WB stages, four-source forwarding and canceled-write replay,\nreal and ALTOPS arithmetic, existing M service schedules, nret=1 and all\npublic ports. Preserve decoder legality, traps, memory bounds, contiguous\nRVFI order, once-only effects, and the existing formal progress window.\nDo not add a cache, predictor policy, instruction specialization or\nbenchmark-dependent behavior. Keep the empty bypass so ready-bus recovery\nand the nine-cycle branch-to-divider retirement bound remain unchanged.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
