{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"agent_message","text":"Capturing PC/immediate substitution before EX raised median Fmax to 76.946 MHz—about 4.17% above the champion, still just below the 4.6% acceptance threshold. I’ll update the hypothesis around this complete operand-capture design and record the measured limit.\n"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_52", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r15s1.yaml')\nh=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nh['title']='Capture complete execution operands before the ID/EX boundary'\nh['motivation']='''The champion scores 182.96 iterations/s at 73.869 MHz and 4,037,538\nCoreMark bracket cycles. Structural queue enlargement and registered\nrecovery failed to clear the acceptance margin; recent paths still traverse\nforwarding and ordinary arithmetic into the memory endpoint. Successful\nr7s1/r8s2 retimed dependency controls but kept data selection inside EX.\nMove the complete operand-delivery network, including PC and immediate\nsubstitution, before the existing ID/EX edge so execution begins directly\nfrom registered ALU and raw architectural operands. Scratch measurements\nshow that partial retiming is insufficient; the complete boundary matters.\n'''\nh['hypothesis']='''Retiming operand delivery is the single structural change. Capture fully\nselected raw rs1/rs2 and dedicated ALU operands exec_a/exec_b at the existing\nID/EX boundary. EX then receives registered operands directly, with no\nEX/MEM or MEM/WB forwarding data mux and no PC/immediate substitution mux\nbefore its fast ALU. Preserve pipeline depth, issue rate, load-use bubbles,\nM service schedules, predictor, fetch queue and in-order retirement.\n\nExpose the current EX instruction's combinational architectural result\nbefore EX/MEM capture: ordinary ALU result, PC+4 link, completed multiplier\nresult or completed divider result. Use the same value that would enter\nEX/MEM.alu_result, without qualifying its data by a late redirect, trap,\nadvance or destination-write permission. At decode, compare each source\nagainst the younger current ID/EX producer using its valid, decoded legal\nwrite intent and nonzero rd. Its result has highest capture priority.\nThis is forwarding from a producer's combinational output into the next\ninstruction's operand register on the same edge the producer advances.\nThere must be no combinational loop: EX arithmetic depends only on its\ncurrent registered operands, never on decode's next operand values.\n\nIf no younger match, capture the current MEM producer when its nonzero\nrd matches and MEM's final write permission is true. Select the existing\nEX/MEM ALU result or MEM's already extracted, sign/zero-extended load word.\nExpose that load word internally without changing the memory protocol or\nMEM/WB banks. Otherwise capture the register-file read value, retaining\nits existing same-cycle WB write-first bypass. MEM permission includes\nvalid, legality and alignment; a faulting load must not hide an older\narchitectural value. x0 never matches a producer. Use mutually exclusive\nRF, EX-result, MEM-ALU and MEM-load lanes before raw operand capture.\n\nRegister dedicated exec_a and exec_b as part of the same ID/EX token.\nFor exec_a, substitute PC for AUIPC; otherwise use the same selected raw\nrs1 source. For exec_b, substitute the decoded immediate for alu_src;\notherwise use selected raw rs2. Fold substitution into the parallel input\nlane enables, adding an exclusive PC or immediate lane. Do not put a\nsubstitution mux after ID/EX, or serially after a completed forwarding mux.\nKeep raw rs1/rs2 separately for branches, stores, JALR, M launch and RVFI.\nThe fast ALU connects directly to exec_a/exec_b. The extra operand storage\nis intentional: the version retaining EX PC/immediate muxes was slower.\n\nRetain the existing youngest-producer permission speculation, now only as\nprovenance tags rather than forwarding data selectors. Register one bit\nper raw source identifying capture from the current EX producer. On the\nfollowing EX cycle validate these tags against EX/MEM's actual reg_write.\nIf a predicted producer canceled its write, replay the consumer PC and\nsuppress its execution, M launch, training, memory effects and retirement,\nexactly as today. Do not move final EX trap permission onto the capture\nmux control path. A canceled younger writer must cause replay even when\nan older matching producer exists; silently using the captured invalid\nresult is wrong. An older MEM source was fully checked before capture.\n\nPreserve the load-use interlock: an immediate dependent consumer cannot\ncapture an EX load's address as its data. It captures the real MEM load\non the following eligible edge. An older dmem stall freezes ID/EX and\nits entire operand/provenance token; unready load data is never captured\nas an advancing consumer. Hold M's original ID/EX instruction until its\nexisting result-completion edge, so decode cannot capture an unfinished\nM result. Preserve launch-time raw operand snapshots and real/ALTOPS\narithmetic. When a launched M instruction holds ID/EX while older stages\ndrain, clear its EX-producer provenance tags once that producer leaves;\nM snapshots remain authoritative and the existing busy-qualified replay\ncheck remains. Never resample a held instruction from the changing queue\nhead. Reset, redirect, load-use flush and invalid-capture priorities stay\nexactly aligned across metadata, raw/ALU operands and provenance tags.\n\nKeep MEM/WB's separate registered ALU/load results, held payload and\nonce-only retirement/writeback semantics. Remove only their direct EX\ndata-forwarding connections. Preserve nret=1, all external ports, illegal\ninstruction defaults, target/alignment traps, memory bounds, stable held\nrequests, contiguous RVFI order and every existing progress assertion.\nNo changes to predictor policy, arithmetic algorithms or evaluation files.\n\nThe complete scratch design, with parallel operand-input lanes and direct\nregistered fast-ALU inputs, measured 76.497/76.946/76.946 MHz across the\nunchanged Gowin placement options: median 76.946 MHz, 6,132 LUT4, 1,985 FF,\nzero LUT-RAM, four BSRAMs and two DSPs. Its divider recurrence became the\nreported worst path. At the expected unchanged 4,037,538 cycles this is\nabout 4.17 percent above the champion, BELOW the 4.6 percent acceptance\nmargin. This demonstrates a useful structural timing change, not a winning\nscore. Forecast five percent with low confidence; final implementation\nstill needs more than 191.37616 iterations/s, about 77.27 MHz at this cycle\ncount. Divider timing, result-output-to-operand-register feedback, added\nstorage and routing can prevent that small remaining clock improvement.\n\nPartial scratch variants were materially worse: capturing only older MEM\nsources measured 62.284 MHz median, and moving every raw bypass before\nID/EX while leaving PC/immediate substitution in EX measured 66.889 MHz.\nExclude those partial implementations. The complete raw-capture variant\npassed all 53 unchanged ALTOPS formal checks, both pipeline test modes,\nreference-ISS cosimulation of selftest and three random programs with and\nwithout bus stalls, and canonical stalled CoreMark at 4,037,538 cycles.\nThe final dedicated-ALU-operand variant has passed both pipeline modes;\nits exact final CoreMark, formal and full cosimulation results must also\nbe checked rather than inferred from the partial version's results.\n\nUpdate internal source-topology tests to assert provenance tags and exact\ncapture lanes, preserving ISA, RVFI and cycle assertions. Cover younger\nEX versus older MEM versus WB writers, simultaneous writers to the same\nregister, x0, every load width/sign, load-use bubbles, canceled writes,\nback-to-back M operations, M launch/drain, and consumers held after their\nolder producers retire. Test AUIPC/immediate substitution independently\nfrom raw store/branch/JALR/M/RVFI operands. Require correct behavior under\nindependent prolonged bus stalls and reset. Run unchanged formal, real\nand ALTOPS pipeline/arithmetic suites, RVFI cosimulation, canonical CRC,\nUART and bracket validation, then the full vendor placement median.\nDeliver only this hypothesis; repository RTL remains unchanged.\n'''\nh['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']=5\nh['changes']=[\n {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Add dedicated exec_a/exec_b words to ID/EX alongside raw source operands; document that all four words are captured before execute and share token hold/flush semantics.'},\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Capture raw sources from mutually exclusive RF, youngest EX-result, older MEM-ALU and older MEM-load lanes. Capture dedicated ALU operands with PC/immediate substitution folded into those lanes. Preserve youngest-writer priority, x0 and exact token capture/hold/flush timing.'},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Use registered exec_a/exec_b directly for the fast ALU and registered raw operands for other execution/RVFI. Expose the current final EX result before its register for decode capture; remove every external data-forwarding and PC/immediate input mux from EX. Keep permission replay, M ownership/snapshots, arithmetic, branch logic and schedules.'},\n {'file':'rtl/forward_unit.sv','description':'Replace data-source vectors with registered youngest-EX-producer provenance tags and the existing actual-write verification/replay request. Tags cannot steer EX data. Preserve predicted intent, hold/flush/reset priorities and tag clearing after producer drain during a launched M wait.'},\n {'file':'rtl/mem_stage.sv','description':'Expose the existing combinational load extraction result internally for ID/EX capture, alongside final producer write permission. Keep memory side effects, width/alignment handling, handshakes and split MEM/WB payload unchanged.'},\n {'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'Wire EX result, MEM load/ALU values and producer identity/permission into decode capture; remove obsolete WB/EX data forwarding and retain provenance verification. Preserve all nret=1 public ports and RVFI behavior.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Adapt source-topology assertions to captured data and provenance tags without weakening correctness, exact cycle or bounded-progress checks. Cover competing writers, source cancellation, load widths, AUIPC/immediate versus raw operands, M ownership/drain, prolonged independent bus stalls and reset in real/ALTOPS modes.'}\n]\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper):pass\ndef text(d,s):\n return d.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None)\nDumper.add_representer(str,text)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(h,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\nprint(p)\nprint('Prototype fitness',76.946e6*10/4037538)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
