{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"The history shows that arithmetic retiming helped, but the core still stops fetching during every load-use, data-memory, and divider stall. I’m proposing a two-entry instruction queue that fetches during those pauses and uses buffered instructions during later instruction-bus stalls. An empty-queue bypass would preserve the current branch-recovery latency.\n\n"}}
