{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md schemas/hypothesis.schema.json'","aggregated_output":"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-002-r1s1 (improvement, +465.59%): Statically removing combinational `/` and `%` from the core ALU and using an eight-cycle shared restoring DIV/REM unit shortened the arithmetic critical path enough for clock gains to outweigh added division stalls in CoreMark.\n- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-001-r2s0 (regression, +37.68%): Four radix-4 steps with registered D/2D/3D and parallel trial subtraction halved div_unit's serial subtract/select depth, raising median Gowin Fmax from 30.789 to 42.390 MHz at unchanged 4,491,485 CoreMark cycles, but a faster retimed divider won the round.\n- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-002-r2s1 (improvement, +50.15%): Folding two narrow restoring steps into launch and moving sign correction to EX/MEM acceptance lets `div_unit` shorten serial subtract/select chains from eight steps to five within the same eight-edge service schedule, improving fitness without adding divider latency.\n- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r2s2 (regression, +12.44%): Tagged next-PC caching reduced control-transfer bubbles and CoreMark cycles by 6.79%, but `div_unit` remained the critical path, leaving its 77.08 iter/s below divider retiming's 102.93 iter/s.\n- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r3s2 (improvement, +11.19%): Deriving direct targets from the fetched instruction enables direction-only recovery with one predicted_taken bit, while raw-instruction decode with valid/ID/EX squashes removes the redirect-to-decode instruction-mask path, letting bimodal prediction improve CoreMark fitness alongside the retimed divider.\n- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-002-r4s1 (improvement, +5.31%): A two-entry fall-through fetch queue lets instructions captured during load-use, dmem and divider holds feed decode when io_imemReady is low, improving stalled CoreMark throughput while preserving immediate decode through the empty-queue bypass.\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
