{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'structural|mul|pipeline|register file|regfile' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Shared combinational divider with fused subtract and compare\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline scores 12.12 at a median 5.442 MHz, and its reported worst\\npath crosses forwarding and the ALU with 156 cells and 199.837 ns arrival\\ntime. The ALU describes signed and unsigned division and remainder with\\nseparate / and % expressions. Their combinational implementation is the\\nstrongest suspected source of the very deep arithmetic path, even when\\nCoreMark executes few divisions. The history contains only the baseline\\nand there is no LESSONS.md or previous divider optimization to reuse.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline scores 12.12 at a median 5.442 MHz, and its reported worst\\npath crosses forwarding and the ALU with 156 cells and 199.837 ns arrival\\ntime. The ALU describes signed and unsigned division and remainder with\\nseparate / and % expressions. Their combinational implementation is the\\nstrongest suspected source of the very deep arithmetic path, even when\\nCoreMark executes few divisions. The history contains only the baseline\\nand there is no LESSONS.md or previous divider optimization to reuse.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU datapath with one explicitly\\nshared, combinational unsigned quotient-and-remainder array, surrounded\\nby RV32M sign conversion and exceptional-result selection. Keep the ALU\\ninterface, zero-cycle combinational latency, pipeline registers, stalls,\\nforwarding, multiplier, and all non-division operations unchanged. This\\nis an arithmetic circuit optimization, with no iterative execution unit\\nor additional pipeline stage.\\n\\nUse 32 statically elaborated restoring steps, from quotient bit 31 down\\nto bit 0. Start R at the unsigned dividend magnitude. At quotient bit k,\\nset W=32-k and subtract divisor[W-1:0] from R[31:k] using an explicitly\\nunsigned W+1-bit subtraction. Accept the subtraction only when its\\nborrow bit is clear and all divisor bits above W-1 are zero; the latter\\n\n…[140566 of 143638 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c4e926a33ccfb42b]…\nhe precise branch-only load-use exemption, source masks and age\\npriority under late correction, raw wrong-path dependencies, imem/dmem\\nstalls and execute_wait. Assert that every other load consumer still\\nreceives its required interlock and held live instructions remain intact.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 115.99, \"delta_pct\": 1.35, \"vs_baseline\": 857.01, \"fmax_mhz\": 47.211, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4070414, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3896, \"ff\": 906, \"seeds\": [45.813, 47.211, 47.211], \"perturbations\": [[0, 45.813, 14], [1, 47.211, 15], [2, 47.211, 15]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -16.828, \"arrival_ns\": 27.122, \"logic_cells\": 14, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 14, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T05:35:12.304153Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 4}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
