{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_47", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml, json, jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r7s1.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261003-002-r7s1',\n'title':'Retiming register-file reads and bypass selection at the decode boundary',\n'category':'structural',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 142.52 iterations/s at 57.541 MHz and 4,037,538\nCoreMark bracket cycles. The latest structural winner removed the major\nM-extension timing limits; the remaining worst path starts in the\nregister file and crosses forwarding and the ordinary ALU. A fresh\nGowin option-0 run reproduced 53.956 MHz and its 23.828 ns path, showing\nthat the inferred register file uses BSRAM. A scratch banked-flop file\nalone reduced median Fmax to 55.748 MHz because register-number\ncomparison through forwarding became critical. Registering dependency\nmatches and using parallel operand selection with the original file\ninstead reached 60.173 MHz, but its 4.57 percent gain falls just short\nof the 4.6 percent acceptance margin. Both paths therefore need the same\nstructural treatment of operand delivery at the decode/execute boundary.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Restructure the integer operand-delivery boundary so register storage\nand dependency comparison both finish before EX's data selection and\narithmetic. Use a banked flop register file with balanced read trees,\nregister forwarding matches alongside ID/EX, and drive parallel one-hot\noperand muxes from those matches. Preserve the existing pipeline depth,\nthroughput, load-use interlock, memory protocol and M-unit schedules.\nThis is one structural operand-delivery hypothesis, with no added stage.\n\nImplement x1..x31 as independently enabled 32-bit flop words, grouped\ninto four banks of eight architectural register numbers; x0 is constant\nzero. Use constant-index word storage, per-word decoded write enables,\nand one-hot masked-OR read trees balanced within and between banks.\nAvoid dynamically indexed inferred memory reads and priority read muxes.\nKeep the existing two combinational read ports, synchronous zero reset,\nwrite-first bypass and ID/EX operand-capture edge. Check mapped storage\nand the retained operand-register boundary in vendor reports.\n\nMove source/destination equality comparisons from EX into the preceding\nID cycle. For each incoming source register, latch two nonzero-destination\nmatch bits: one against the current ID/EX destination, which becomes\nEX/MEM on that edge, and one against the current EX/MEM destination,\nwhich becomes MEM/WB. The four match bits travel with the instruction.\nQualify these matches in EX with the actual current producer reg_write\ncontrols, preserving EX/MEM-over-MEM/WB priority. Register matches, not\nspeculatively assumed producer write permission: misaligned accesses or\ncontrol transfers can still suppress a producer's architectural write.\n\nReset or a permitted ID/EX flush clears the match state. On normal ID/EX\ncapture recompute it from the selected fetch-queue head and pre-edge\nproducer destinations. A dmem hold retains both sets of match bits,\nmatching the held EX/MEM and retained MEM/WB forwarding payload. When\nID/EX is held for an M operation but older stages advance, transfer the\nold EX-match bits into the WB-match bits and clear EX matches as EX/MEM\nbecomes a bubble. Never recompute a held instruction's matches from a\nchanging queue head. Load-use bubbles, redirects, invalid instructions,\nand simultaneous hold/flush priorities must mirror ID/EX exactly.\nKeep retained WB forwarding qualified by its stored reg_write, not by\nretirement-valid, which intentionally clears during a dmem hold.\n\nProduce mutually exclusive RF, EX/MEM and MEM/WB enables for each source.\nSelect source data with parallel masked-OR logic, avoiding encoded\npriority-mux cascades. Form ALU operands directly from those sources\nplus PC or immediate with mutually exclusive enables, so AUIPC/immediate\nselection does not add another serial data mux after forwarding.\nKeep separate correct raw rs1/rs2 selections for branch comparisons,\nstores, JALR, M-unit launch and RVFI; immediate or PC substitution must\nnot change architectural source reporting. Preserve M-unit captured\noperands, reset cancellation, once-only completion and downstream bypass.\n\nPreserve nret=1, all top-level ports, the fetch queue and predictor,\ndecoder legality, memory alignment traps and side-effect gating,\ncontiguous retirement, and every formal/progress/arithmetic assertion.\nForecast a 10 percent fitness gain at unchanged bracket cycles; this\nrequires about 63.30 MHz. Acceptance requires over 149.07592 iterations/s,\nor about 60.19 MHz at 4,037,538 cycles. Additional flop/read-tree area,\nwrite fanout and the remaining arithmetic paths are the main risks.\nMeasure median vendor Gowin Fmax times the actual bracketed cycle rate.\nRun unchanged formal, full RVFI cosimulation, real/ALTOPS pipeline tests,\nand canonical stalled CoreMark CRC/UART/marker checks. Prototype data\nfor the individual changes motivates the combined hypothesis; it is\nnot yet a measurement of the combined design.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':10,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/reg_file.sv','description':'''Use 31 constant-index flop words and two balanced one-hot read trees,\ngrouped four by eight, with x0 constant. Preserve synchronous reset,\nwrite-first bypass, independent read ports and all interface semantics.\nEnsure synthesis no longer implements this file with inferred BSRAM.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/forward_unit.sv','description':'''Register four ID-stage nonzero destination matches using clock/reset,\nID hold/flush and EX/MEM hold inputs. Advance matches with their producer\nstages during M waits; retain them on dmem holds. Gate stored matches\nwith actual producer write controls and emit mutually exclusive RF,\nEX/MEM and MEM/WB enables with youngest-writer priority. Remove the\nobsolete EX-stage address comparisons and unused destination inputs.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Wire queue-head sources, ID/EX and EX/MEM destinations and pipeline\nhold/flush controls to the registered forwarding unit. Carry one-hot\nsource enables into EX. Keep memory/RVFI IO, retirement width and all\nexisting stage/handshake connections unchanged.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Use parallel one-hot operand networks for raw rs1/rs2. Build ALU a/b\nwith PC/immediate eligibility folded into source enables rather than\nserial muxes after forwarding. Preserve raw operands for stores,\nbranches, JALR, M-unit launch and RVFI; retain all arithmetic latencies,\ntrap handling, correction qualification and stall/accept behavior.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_reg_file.py','description':'''Keep existing tests and add exhaustive address-pair reads of distinct\nper-register values, simultaneous bypass on both ports, randomized\nwrites/reads, x0 writes, bank boundaries and reset of populated state.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Preserve every existing test. Exercise competing same-destination\nproducers, WB-to-ID bypass, cross-bank dependencies, both-source matches,\nload-use bubbles, memory holds overlapping MUL/DIV, held WB forwarding,\nmisaligned producer write suppression, and redirects/reset with pending\nmatches. Check raw RVFI source values, results, order and once-only\nmemory effects in real and ALTOPS modes; retain all progress bounds.\n'''}]}\nclass D(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\nD.add_representer(str,lambda dumper,s: dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None))\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=D,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Revised hypothesis is schema-valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
