{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_42", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor s in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n x=json.loads(s)\n if x['id']=='hyp-20261003-002-r3s1':\n  print(x['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\n  print(x.get('critical_path'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Restructure the existing front-end pipeline around independently clocked\nvalidity and payload state. A squash changes whether an instruction may\nexecute; it need not rewrite that instruction or its operand data. Keep\nthe existing stage boundaries, single issue, branch resolution point and\ndivider service schedule. The single architectural change is separating\ntoken validity from payload transport and its hazard-control consumers.\n\nMake the IF instruction payload the unmasked imem_data. Neither redirect\nnor imem-not-ready may mux its bits to a NOP before decode, immediate\ngeneration, register-file addresses or load-use comparisons. Convey the\nunavailable/squashed status separately through validity and kill control.\nPreserve the PC register's redirect-over-stall priority and reset vector.\nThe memory interface still accepts instructions only when imemReady is\nhigh and the pipeline can consume them; raw unavailable bus data is never\nan architectural instruction.\n\nSplit ID/EX validity updates from payload updates. Reset clears validity;\na permitted redirect or load-use bubble clears only validity. Otherwise\nhold validity on dmem/execute/load-use interlock, or capture fetch validity\nwhen advancing. Keep the existing precedence: dmem backpressure and a\npending division retain the active ID/EX instruction, while load-use\ninserts a bubble when not overridden by those holds. Payload registers\nmay capture raw decode and register-file values whenever the stage is\nnot held, including a squash edge, or retain old values while held.\nDo not put redirect, flush or