{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_64", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r8s1.yaml');x=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nx['title']='Retime the complete producer-to-memory bypass path'\nx['motivation']='''The champion scores 173.56 iterations/s at 70.074 MHz and 4,037,538 CoreMark bracket cycles. Its reported worst path starts at EX/MEM producer write control and reaches data-memory BSRAM through forwarding and the general ALU. The previous structural winner moved register-file reads and dependency matches before ID/EX, but producer qualification, WB result selection and address generation still share the same downstream timing cone. Scratch isolation experiments show that removing just one segment exposes another: separate address generation alone reached 62.905 MHz, registered forwarding enables 65.910 MHz, and registered enables plus WB data 67.723 MHz on placement option 1. Combining those register-boundary changes with a dedicated address register reached 71.148 MHz on option 1. This identifies a coordinated bypass-path restructuring rather than a new pipeline stage as the promising structural angle.'''\nx['hypothesis']=x['hypothesis'].replace('Complete the forwarding network\\\\'s existing register boundaries:', 'Restructure the producer-to-memory bypass path at its existing register boundaries:')\nx['hypothesis']=x['hypothesis'].replace('Keep the pipeline depth, all instruction service schedules and the load-use interlock unchanged.', 'Add a dedicated memory-address result path with late source selection, completing the removal of serial producer-control and general-result selection from the memory endpoint. Keep the pipeline depth, all instruction service schedules and the load-use interlock unchanged.')\ninsert='''Partition load/store address execution from the general ALU result. Compute three full-width 32-bit address candidates in parallel: ID/EX.rs1_val + imm, EX/MEM.alu_result + imm, and the unified MEM/WB.writeback_value + imm. Select among completed sums with the registered mutually exclusive rs1 source enables, then capture a dedicated EX/MEM.effective_addr on the existing edge. Thus forwarding-source control selects completed addresses rather than entering the carry-propagation cone. This is the final segment of the same bypass-path retiming, with no speculative memory requests. Do not use AUIPC substitution, ALU operand-B selection or MUL/DIV/link result selection in this path. Retain the general alu_result for register writeback and arithmetic forwarding. Use effective_addr for the bus address, alignment, byte masks, load extraction and RVFI aligned memory address. Preserve full 32-bit carries, signed immediates, dmem hold stability, and existing reset/zero-control bubble priorities.\n\n'''\nx['hypothesis']=x['hypothesis'].replace('Preserve nret=1, top-level IO,',insert+'Preserve nret=1, top-level IO,')\nx['hypothesis']=x['hypothesis'].replace('The forecast is ten percent, requiring approximately 77.08 MHz.','The forecast is eight percent, requiring approximately 75.68 MHz.')\nx['hypothesis']=x['hypothesis'].replace('Combined-design timing and correctness validation are still pending.','The registered-enable/unified-WB subset passed all 53 unchanged formal checks. The final replicated-address version still needs complete validation; the 71.148 MHz intermediate result by itself is below the required acceptance margin.')\nx['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'}\nfor c in x['changes']:\n if c['file']=='rtl/ex_stage.sv':c['description']+=' Add three parallel source-specific rs1-plus-immediate adders; select their outputs with the registered one-hot rs1 source vector and capture effective_addr on the existing EX/MEM edge. Preserve full-width arithmetic and all hold/reset/bubble rules.'\n if c['file']=='rtl/core_pkg.sv':c['description']+=' Add independent 32-bit effective_addr to ex_mem_t; preserve alu_result for forwarding and writeback.'\n if c['file']=='rtl/mem_stage.sv':c['description']+=' Drive memory address-dependent functions, including bus address, lane masks, alignment checks, load extraction and RVFI address, from effective_addr. Keep ordinary result forwarding separate.'\n if c['file']=='test/test_pipeline.py':c['description']+=' Exercise all three address candidate sources, signed offsets, carries, every memory width, MMIO, misalignment and stalls; assert only the selected address reaches the bus.'\njsonschema.validate(x,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()));p.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(x,sort_keys=False,width=86));print('VALID')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
