{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_38", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r9s1.yaml')\nh=dict(id='hyp-20261003-002-r9s1',title='Compare branch source candidates before forwarding selection',category='structural',motivation='''The champion scores 182.96 iterations/s at 73.869 MHz and 4,037,538 bracketed CoreMark cycles. A reproduction of placement option 1 confirms a critical path from a forwarding selector through two operand-mux levels, the branch comparison carry chain, redirect qualification and ID/forwarding reset. The recent registered operand-source predictions accelerated ALU delivery but the branch still compares already-multiplexed 32-bit values. Previous delayed recovery added cycles without sufficient clock benefit; the next structural opportunity is replicated branch evaluation with late one-bit selection and no new stage.''',hypothesis='''Restructure the conditional-branch execution path as a bank of parallel candidate comparisons followed by selection of the comparison result. For each of the four existing rs1 source candidates and four rs2 candidates, compute equality and unsigned less-than directly from the source words, before applying forwarding enables. The candidates are captured ID/EX raw register values, EX/MEM ALU result, MEM/WB ALU result and MEM/WB extended load result. Keep the existing registered four-way one-hot forwarding predictions and their youngest-writer/x0 rules unchanged. Compute signed less-than by selecting the first operand sign when signs differ and unsigned less-than otherwise. Select equality for BEQ/BNE, signed less-than for BLT/BGE, unsigned less-than for BLTU/BGEU, and invert for the complementary operation. Gate each one-bit candidate predicate with its rs1 and rs2 source enables and reduce the terms with a balanced OR tree.\n\nThis is a structural duplication-and-selection change to the branch execution unit. The forwarding selectors now choose one-bit branch decisions after comparison instead of selecting 32-bit inputs before comparison. Shared-source pairs may collapse to known equality/ordering results and symmetric comparisons may share logic if semantics are preserved. Keep explicit source candidates visible to synthesis; do not reintroduce a wide selected-operand comparator as the only realized implementation. Preserve raw rs1/rs2 muxes for stores, JALR, M launches and RVFI and the current ALU operand paths. Do not alter arithmetic-unit schedules, branch resolution stage, predictor policy/training timing, fetch queue, load-use interlock or pipeline depth.\n\nFeed the selected exact branch predicate into the existing branch_taken, actual_taken, trap and correction equations. Keep branch target alignment and full-width target arithmetic, replay precedence, ex_advance gating and once-only training unchanged. Canceled selected producer writes still suppress execution and replay the consumer before any architectural effect. An invalid or flushed source vector must not permit side effects; M snapshots and retained WB payloads continue using their current rules. This computes actual comparisons, not guessed branch outcomes; no new prediction state or recovery mode is required.\n\nForecast eight percent fitness improvement with low confidence at unchanged CoreMark cycles. Acceptance requires median Gowin Fmax above 77.27 MHz at 4,037,538 cycles. Replicated comparators increase LUT/carry resources and routing demand, and ordinary ALU or divider paths may become limiting; a shorter logical selector path alone does not establish a gain. Measure the mapped circuit and the median Fmax times measured iterations/cycle. The candidate must fit the Tang Nano 20K and retain the 10,000-LUT target. Do not combine this with a different predictor, cache or arithmetic redesign.\n\nPreserve all existing tests and checks, including the nine-cycle ready-bus branch-to-divider retirement-gap bound and formal liveness window. Add targeted coverage of all six branch operations over realizable RF/EX/WB-ALU/WB-load source pairings, equal operands, unsigned boundaries and opposite signs, competing same-register writers, x0, load-use stalls, retained WB during dmem holds and canceled-link replay. Compare architectural RVFI source values as well as outcomes and PCs; preserve once-only memory effects and contiguous retirement. Run full real/ALTOPS pipeline tests, unchanged formal and stalled RVFI cosimulation, canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/marker validation and vendor timing. Keep nret=1 and every public IO, trap/decoder rule and bounded address requirement. Deliver only the hypothesis; repository RTL is unchanged.''',expected_impact=dict(fitness_delta_pct=8,confidence='low'),changes=[dict(file='rtl/ex_stage.sv',description='Build parallel branch comparison predicates directly from all four raw source candidates per operand, then mask and OR their one-bit results using the existing registered forwarding vectors. Preserve raw operands, ALU and M paths, exact branch/jump alignment and redirects, replay priority and all pipeline registers and service schedules.'),dict(file='test/test_pipeline.py',description='Add architectural branch tests spanning all six predicates and realizable forwarding-source pairs, signed/unsigned boundaries, equal values, x0, competing writers, load-use bubbles, retained WB, dmem/imem holds, canceled selected writes and branch-to-DIV progress. Keep all existing tests, cycle bounds and exact RVFI/side-effect checks in both real and ALTOPS builds.')])\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=82))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Revised hypothesis is schema valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
