{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_64", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r9s1.yaml')\nh=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nh['title']='Retime branch resolution controls across the ID/EX boundary'\nh['motivation']='''The champion scores 182.96 iterations/s at 73.869 MHz with 4,037,538 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Reproducing Gowin placement option 1 confirms a critical path from a forwarding selector through operand selection, a branch comparison carry chain, redirect qualification and the ID/forwarding reset network. Earlier operand retiming removed late bypass qualification, leaving this branch-control feedback path exposed. Registering recovery after EX previously added cycles without sufficient clock benefit. Instead, move operand-independent branch resolution work before the existing ID/EX edge while retaining the current EX resolution cycle.'''\nh['hypothesis']='''Partition conditional-branch resolution into registered static control in ID and dynamic operand comparisons in EX. At the existing ID/EX capture edge, register one-hot controls for the six legal branch predicates, one-hot controls for the predicate that means the captured prediction is wrong, and branch-training eligibility derived from the direct target alignment. This is one structural retiming of the branch-control boundary; it neither adds a pipeline stage nor changes prediction policy, fetch buffering, forwarding selection, ALU/M service schedules or retirement width.\n\nFor a validated branch, form six outcome enables for EQ, NE, signed LT, signed GE, unsigned LT and unsigned GE. For an aligned direct target, form the corresponding six recovery enables after XORing branch_op bit zero with this token's predicted_taken bit. Thus a predicted-not-taken BEQ requests correction on EQ, while a predicted-taken BEQ requests correction on NE; the same complementary pairing applies to signed and unsigned comparisons. All other recovery enables are zero. For a misaligned direct target, actual_taken must be false whether or not the comparison succeeds, so record a separate forced-fallthrough recovery bit equal to predicted_taken. Keep default-illegal decoding unchanged; nonbranches and invalid decode entries must not acquire branch enables.\n\nAlso register two mutually exclusive training classes for legal branches: aligned target, which can train for either outcome, and misaligned target, which may train only if the condition is false. The latter preserves the existing rule that an untaken branch does not fault merely because its encoded target is misaligned. Compute the target alignment from the full-width PC-plus-immediate semantics in ID. Do not truncate architectural targets or wrap addresses. Register only the small control metadata; retain current target and PC+4 datapaths in EX rather than adding wide target registers to this proposal.\n\nIn EX retain the current forwarded raw rs1/rs2 operands and compare them once for equality, signed less-than and unsigned less-than. Form complementary predicates and use parallel masked-OR selection with the registered outcome controls. Independently select the prediction-error predicate with the registered recovery controls. This bypasses the current serial branch-op selection, taken qualification, misalignment qualification and predicted_taken XOR on the common aligned-branch recovery path. Use the outcome for branch_taken and RVFI next-PC/trap semantics, and use the separate error result only to request the existing correction. Training uses its registered eligibility classes and the actual condition. Preserve pre-edge counter lookup, same-index training behavior and once-per-advancing-branch updates.\n\nQualify branch correction by the valid token, reset, older dmem hold and operand-prediction verification. Since the recovery controls are nonzero only for legal conditional branches, do not serialize branch correction through an unrelated M-unit completion cone. Keep ordinary JAL/JALR and nonbranch prediction correction separate, including JALR bit-zero clearing and target alignment. Factor nonbranch actual-taken logic from jump legality/alignment directly, without depending on a conditional-branch comparison that cannot belong to that instruction. Canceled selected producer writes retain highest correction priority: replay the consumer PC and suppress its branch training, memory effects, arithmetic launch and retirement. The existing actual branch/jump target and correction target selection remain architectural and full-width.\n\nMove the metadata with exactly the existing ID/EX reset, flush, hold, invalid-capture and normal-capture priorities. Retain zero-control bubbles and zero forwarding selectors where the existing tests require them. Hold captured predicted_taken and the new controls together through dmem and execute holds. Preserve source snapshots, retained MEM/WB forwarding and every existing side-effect qualification. No delayed branch recovery, early speculative memory operation or extra replay mode is introduced.\n\nForecast five percent fitness improvement with low confidence, at unchanged 4,037,538 bracket cycles. Acceptance requires median Gowin Fmax above approximately 77.27 MHz; a five percent gain needs approximately 77.56 MHz. This is an unproven forecast. Partial scratch variants passed all 37 existing pipeline tests in each real/ALTOPS mode but did not clear the acceptance margin: registering recovery controls plus wide target/PC4 payloads measured 72.057 MHz median, and the smaller recovery-only variant measured 68.839 MHz. Those partial variants are not winning evidence. The final proposal additionally retimes outcome and training controls and separates the jump correction cone, targeting remaining serial branch qualification rather than relying on placement noise. Its final implementation must be judged by measured median vendor Fmax times actual iteration/cycle rate; ordinary ALU/divider timing and extra control fanout may prevent a win.\n\nRun the unchanged formal checks, full real/ALTOPS pipeline suites, stalled RVFI cosimulation and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/marker validation. Preserve the existing nine-cycle ready-bus branch-to-divider gap assertion and formal liveness window. Test every legal branch predicate and prediction direction, signed/unsigned boundaries, all forwarding sources, misaligned targets for taken and untaken outcomes, illegal branch encodings, JAL/JALR faults, canceled-write replay, independent bus stalls and reset. Require exact RVFI operands, trap/PC/order and once-only memory effects. Preserve nret=1, all public IO, every decoder/trap rule and bounded address requirement; do not change evaluation files or weaken checks. Deliver only this hypothesis with repository RTL unchanged.'''\nh['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':5,'confidence':'low'}\nh['changes']=[{'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Extend id_ex_t with six one-hot branch outcome enables, six one-hot recovery enables plus a forced-fallthrough bit, and two branch-training eligibility bits. Preserve all existing fields, widths, top-level IO and downstream bundles.'},{'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Derive the small branch outcome/recovery/training controls from positively decoded branch type, token predicted_taken and direct-target alignment. Register them on the existing ID/EX edge with exactly its reset/flush/hold/invalid priorities. Keep ordinary decode legality and payload behavior; do not add a stage or wide target registers.'},{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Consume registered branch controls with parallel masked selection of actual equality/signed/unsigned comparison predicates. Separate prediction-error selection from actual outcome and training qualification, and factor jump correction independently. Preserve targets, trap and replay precedence, source forwarding, M-unit schedules, side-effect suppression and immediate advancing-EX recovery.'},{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Retain all current tests and cycle bounds. Add branch metadata hold/flush and all predicate/prediction combinations, taken versus untaken misaligned targets, signed/unsigned boundaries, each forwarding source, canceled writes, JALR faults, backpressure, reset and branch/replay followed by DIV/REM. Check exact RVFI and once-only effects in real and ALTOPS builds.'}]\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=82));jsonschema.validate(h,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Final structural candidate written and schema validated')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
