{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_76", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json, yaml, jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r10s2.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nh=d['hypothesis']\nh=h.replace('In parallel compute the exact branch condition from full architectural forwarded operands. A split implementation may select low-byte ordering when the upper 24 bits are equal, otherwise signed/unsigned upper-24 ordering.', 'In parallel compute the exact branch condition from full architectural forwarded operands. Use the original native full-width equality and signed/unsigned comparisons in this validation path; do not require a serial upper-equality/upper-order/low-order selection network. The low-byte comparator supplies speculation only.')\nh=h.replace('Preserve exact once-only training from the validated outcome; never train using the narrow speculative result.', '''Move conditional-branch training for ALL branch kinds to EX/MEM, using the already registered exact branch_taken, PC and effective trap status. Train once when that branch transfers from EX/MEM to MEM/WB, excluding correction_service, reset and holds. A retained correcting branch trains on its later normal transfer, not on the service edge. Never train on a younger squashed branch or from the narrow speculative result. This removes the full comparison from counter-update feedback as well as immediate redirect. Prediction table size and policy stay unchanged, but training arrives one cycle later; carry the original fetched predicted_taken bit, and preserve pre-edge lookup semantics. Update cycle-accurate predictor scoreboards to model this explicitly, retaining every architectural and table-transition assertion.''')\nh=h.replace('Use actual full-operand outcomes for RVFI and traps, including taken misaligned branches.', '''Bound every new speculative taken path. Reuse IF's full-width PC-plus-direct-immediate eligibility calculation, independently of the direction counter, and carry one direct_target_eligible bit with the exact token through both queue entries, if_id_t and id_ex_t. Eligibility requires word-aligned source and target PCs in [0, 0x00100000), after full-width addition. An ordered branch may use a speculative taken narrow result only when this saved bit is true; otherwise speculate fall-through and let registered exact validation repair any real transfer. Do not compute this bounds predicate after the EX comparator, truncate targets, or confuse eligibility with predicted_taken. This prevents an actually untaken branch with an out-of-range target from causing a new speculative out-of-bounds fetch.\n\nUse actual full-operand outcomes for RVFI and traps, including taken misaligned branches.''')\nh=h.replace('Forecast 7 percent higher fitness', 'Forecast 6 percent higher fitness')\nh += '''\n\nExperimental limits: an 8-bit speculative prototype retaining EX-stage exact training passed all 53 unchanged formal checks and existing pipeline suites, validated canonical CoreMark, and measured 4,055,597 bracket cycles at 71.136/72.268/72.268 MHz (median 72.268), approximately 178.19 iter/s. A 16-bit version with saved target eligibility measured 4,056,188 cycles and 69.816 MHz median; it passed all 53 formal checks and existing pipeline/fetch suites after only updating their packed-field offsets. BOTH are below the 182.96 champion. Neither demonstrates the forecast. The final proposal retains the more promising 8-bit fast path, adds mandatory target eligibility, restores native full-width validation mapping and moves exact training to the registered branch boundary. This final combination has not been measured or fully verified. Its clock advantage is uncertain because the prototype's next limiting paths were the divider and ALU-to-memory paths. Implementation must pass the unchanged gates and demonstrate the required fitness gain; do not present the scratch measurements as an improvement.'''\nd['hypothesis']=h\nd['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']=6\nfor c in d['changes']:\n if c['file']=='rtl/ex_stage.sv':\n  c['description'] += ''' Use the captured target-eligibility bit to bound speculative taken redirects. Use native full-width relations for exact validation. Drive branch_train/index/outcome from the exact registered EX/MEM branch on its transfer to WB, excluding correction_service, reset and holds, rather than from the live EX comparator. All exact comparison consumers must terminate in registered validation or RVFI data, not re-enter same-cycle correction through training qualification.'''\n if c['file']=='test/test_pipeline.py':\n  c['description'] += ''' Adjust packed-bundle extraction for the added eligibility bit and make the cycle-accurate predictor model consume exact registered training at the MEM/WB transfer boundary. Preserve the existing comparisons, pre-edge semantics and all architectural assertions. Add actually-untaken ordered branches whose narrow result says taken but whose direct targets overflow, underflow or cross the one-megabyte boundary; assert no speculative out-of-range fetch.'''\nd['changes'][2:2]=[\n {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Add direct_target_eligible to if_id_t and id_ex_t, retaining predicted_taken and all architectural metadata. Top-level RVFI shape and nret remain unchanged.'},\n {'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'Expose the existing full-width direct-target alignment/range predicate independently of direction prediction. Store that bit with each complete fetch token, including the fall-through bypass and both queue entries, so EX can bound newly speculative branch choices without a late address-validity cone. Keep counter initialization, saturating transitions, raw decode, queue and redirect priorities; accept exact registered branch training through the existing ports.'},\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Capture and hold the selected token\\\\'s direct_target_eligible with ID/EX under the existing reset, flush, bubble and hold rules.'},\n {'file':'test/test_if_stage.py','description':'Update packed-bundle offsets for the eligibility bit while retaining every existing fetch, queue, prediction and counter assertion. Add independent checks that eligibility matches the full source/target alignment and range calculation regardless of direction-table state, survives queue holds and is discarded with squashed tokens.'}\n]\nclass BlockDumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef represent_text(dumper, value):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',value,style='|' if '\\\\n' in value or len(value)>140 else None)\nBlockDumper.add_representer(str,represent_text)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=BlockDumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert d['id']=='hyp-20261003-003-r10s2' and d['category']=='predictor'\nassert type(d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int and -50<=d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']<=50\nprint('Validated',p)\nprint('Changes:', ', '.join(c['file'] for c in d['changes']))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
