{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_37", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r12s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261003-003-r12s2\ntitle: \"Reduce conditional-direction aliasing with a banked hashed bimodal predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion still uses only 64 untagged two-bit direction counters,\n  indexed by PC[7:2], so conditional branches separated by 256 bytes can\n  repeatedly overwrite one another's learned bias. Recent changes to\n  correction timing have regressed, and r11s2's target-cache proposal\n  timed out in formal. Improve direction accuracy while retaining the\n  proven immediate-derived targets and same-cycle direction-only recovery.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the 64-entry direction table with one 256-entry, two-bit\n  saturating bimodal table indexed by PC[9:2] XOR PC[17:10]. Apply exactly\n  the same hash to fetch lookup and advancing EX training. This is a\n  single direction-predictor change: spread hot branches across more\n  counters without adding speculative history, target prediction or a\n  pipeline stage. Initialize counters to weakly not-taken as before.\n\n  Bank the table into sixteen banks of sixteen entries, with shallow\n  local reads and a balanced bank-output selection. Separate prediction\n  MSBs from hysteresis LSBs if this improves Gowin mapping; the fetch\n  path needs only one bit per entry. Preserve a single training write\n  per cycle and pre-edge lookup semantics for simultaneous read/write.\n  Update the current counter, not a fetch-time counter snapshot, with\n  exact saturating arithmetic. Bank enables must not create serial\n  priority logic. Do not reset payloads through a global wide mux.\n\n  Keep legal fetched-instruction recognition, full-width immediate target\n  arithmetic, alignment and one-megabyte speculative-target bounds,\n  JAL prediction, JALR handling and the one-bit predicted_taken metadata\n  unchanged. Both queue entries and the empty-queue bypass must retain\n  the exact prediction used when their token was accepted. Train only\n  on the existing ex_advance-qualified legal, nonfaulting branch event;\n  holds, bubbles, resets, operand replays and squashed\n…[1220 of 4292 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:81b7aaadd3e46f1a]…\nOR PC[17:10].\n      Preserve branch_train, branch_outcome, direction-only correction,\n      operand replay, full-width architectural targets and trap behavior.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Widen only the internal branch_index connection between EX and IF.\n      Preserve all top-level ports and the nret=1 retirement contract.\n  - file: test/test_if_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Adapt the independent direction-table model to the new size/hash,\n      retaining every queue, prediction, range and saturation assertion.\n      Add old-index collision pairs with opposite biases, new-index\n      collisions, bank boundaries and same-edge lookup/training cases.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Update predictor-policy expectations without relaxing architectural\n      assertions. Exercise aliasing branches with bus stalls, full queues,\n      M holds and operand replay; check single training per advancing\n      branch and precise RVFI PC, trap, order and wrong-path suppression.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
