\nInitialize counter and kind on every allocation before marking valid.\\nUse generic synthesizable arrays and no new source-list dependency.\\n\\nA valid tag hit predicts its cached target for unconditional transfers\\nor when a conditional counter's MSB is one; otherwise predict PC+4.\\nJAL and JALR share unconditional entries, with JALR using its last\\nresolved target. Misses predi\n…[6196 of 9268 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e6c03199b854ab1b]…\ning integration suite with warm taken loops and\\nexits, forward branches, JAL links, repeated and changing JALR\\ntargets, two full PCs colliding at one index, cold/reset behavior,\\nand stale hits after replacing code at a trained PC. Exercise both\\ncorrection directions, reserved branch/JALR encodings, misaligned\\ntargets and out-of-range speculative targets without issuing an\\nactual out-of-range architectural access. Test branches dependent\\non loads, older stalled memory operations, simultaneous imem/dmem\\nstalls at correction, and DIV/REM on a predicted successor path.\\nCheck held instructions train at most once, unfinished division\\nnever corrects, RVFI successors/orders and links are exact, and\\nsquashed stores/retirements never occur. Include same-index lookup\\nand training on one edge, no allocation on not-taken misses,\\ncorrect-prediction successor retention,\\nand a ready-bus warm loop that demonstrates removed fetch bubbles.\\nRetain every existing assertion and use ready-aware memory stimuli.\\n'}]}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
