{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_19", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id']=='hyp-20261003-001-r12s0':\n  h=d['hypothesis'];print(h['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Separate validity and side-effect controls from the wide fetch-queue, ID/EX and EX/MEM payload update conditions. Let payload data capture whenever its stage is not held, even when the token is invalid, flushed or waiting for an M result. This is one control-fanout and input-mux micro-optimization applied consistently to the existing payload register boundaries. There is no extra pipeline stage, changed instruction latency, new speculation policy or altered branch comparator.\n\nIn id_stage retain synchronous reset of the complete bundle. Otherwise update valid with the exact existing priorities: flush clears it even when stalled; stall retains it; ordinary capture takes in.valid. All other fields, including decoded controls, capture the current raw selected token whenever !stall, independent of flush and in.valid. During stall they retain their previous values. Never introduce decode_accept or a bubble-dependent payload enable, since those would restore the late recovery path. Qualify the core hazard connection's id_ex_mem_read with id_ex_w.valid, because invalid ID/EX payload may contain a load. Retain the existing valid qualification on producer write intent and all executing-instruction consumers.\n\nIn ex_stage retain reset clearing and dmem-stall holding of the complete EX/MEM register. On every other edge capture ALL non-control payload fields unconditionally using their existing expressions: PC, ALU/M/link result, raw store operand, register addresses, forwarded RVFI operands, resolved PC/branch metadata and instruction. Independently, clear ctrl and valid when operands_invalid || execute_wait || !in.valid; otherwise capture ctrl_with_trap and in.valid. Do not retain inactive payload on a bubble: that would put execute_wait, replay or validity back on its write enable. Valid and side-effect controls must still become zero on every bubble, replay and incomplete M operation. Early captures of an incomplete M result are harmless only with those controls and valid cleared; the actual completion edge still capture\n…[4118 of 7190 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:dc08013bfdd85883]…\ne estimate is a hypothesis, not an achieved score; judge the complete prescribed Gowin placement median. Deliver only this hypothesis file; scratch prototypes do not alter repository RTL.\n\nA scratch precursor changing only ID/EX and EX/MEM payload updates measured 73.196 MHz in vendor placement option 1 with 5,202 LUT4 and 1,929 FF, below both champion and acceptance threshold. Its worst path moved to fetch queue payload enables (head_q.instr), which still depended on recovery. This is negative evidence, not a gain. The final proposal includes the explicit IF payload-write separation above; its full three-option timing and correctness gates remain required. The forecast is low confidence.\n\nAn independent queue-transition model checked all 48 combinations of old occupancy, instruction-bus readiness, downstream hold, redirect and reset. The new payload-write rules preserved every live token under the unchanged occupancy transitions. This validates the queue algorithm only, not the RTL or full-core correctness.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
