bled by is_div; MUL result by is_mul; PC+4 by\n!is_m && in.ctrl.is_jump; fast ALU result by\n!is_m && !in.ctrl.is_jump. Combine with a balanced OR expression.\nPreserve the existing valid/illegal qualification of is_div/is_mul,\nexact trap behavior and the advancing EX/MEM edge and backpressure.\n\nRemove bubble clearing from wide EX/MEM payload inputs. On reset\nstill clear the entire bundle; on dmem stall retain it. Otherwise,\nwhen execute_wait || !in.valid, clear only reg_q.ctrl and reg_q.valid\nand retain every other payload fie\n…[14280 of 17352 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:cfcf8aeffab591ad]…\nid tokens containing LOAD, STORE, branch, JALR\nand M encodings, load-use bubbles, wrong-path producer matches,\ncanceled-write replay, reset, full fetch queues and long bus holds.\nAssert that stale invalid controls cannot stall indefinitely, launch an\nM operation, redirect/train, request memory, write a register or retire.\nSource-mask zero is no longer a required representation for an invalid\ntoken; retain all architectural, latency and progress assertions.\n\nRun unchanged formal and RVFI cosimulation gates and canonical stalled\nCoreMark CRC/UART/marker validation. Expect exactly 4,037,538 bracket\ncycles with the same inputs. Acceptance requires more than 191.37616\niterations/s, approximately 77.27 MHz at that cycle count. Forecast a\nseven-percent fitness gain with low confidence. Divider recurrence,\nALU feedback or remaining redirect-to-PC/valid paths may cap the gain;\nvendor mapping could also offset lower fanout. This forecast is not a\nmeasured improvement; judge the full prescribed Gowin placement median.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
