{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_75","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r13s2.yaml');d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\na='Use one asynchronous lookup port and one synchronous training write port. Keep reset to weakly not taken (01), with reset priority over writes, using synthesis-friendly storage. Check Gowin mapping rather than assuming a small array becomes RAM. A logical reset implementation may use validity and default 01 if needed, but every invalid entry must read a defined 01 immediately after reset and every first write must install the complete state. Do not scrub entries over extra cycles or weaken reset checks.'\nb='''Use one asynchronous lookup port and one synchronous training write port, explicitly implemented as two banks of sixteen entries. Split the two state bits into independent unreset one-bit memory planes in each bank (four 16x1 arrays total). Index[4] chooses the bank and index[3:0] the word; enable writes to exactly one bank and write both planes atomically. Use a separate 32-bit resettable valid bitmap. Logical lookup is stored state when valid, otherwise 01; reset clears all validity in one edge and suppresses training. First training initializes both data planes before their validity becomes visible. Saturating writes use the saved logical snapshot, so they never consult uninitialized storage. No data-array reset or reset mux may remain on the memory write path. This concrete organization is intended to map to distributed RAM16, not BSRAM or resettable counter-word flops. Check the vendor mapping; do not assume inference from RTL size. Do not scrub entries over extra cycles or weaken reset checks.'''\nassert a in d['hypothesis'];d['hypothesis']=d['hypothesis'].replace(a,b)\nd['hypothesis']+='''\\\\n\\\\nExperimental limit: a snapshot-trained precursor using a resettable 32x2 array passed the canonical CoreMark validator with all CRCs, no out-of-bounds access and 4,034,312 bracket cycles. Placement option 1 reached only 70.947 MHz, using 5,114 LUT4, 1,871 registers and zero RAM16 resources. It did not achieve the intended storage inference and is a regression, not evidence of the forecast. The final proposal therefore requires the unreset banked bit planes and reset-valid lookup above. That final storage implementation has not been timed or formally checked during hypothesis generation. Full formal and the three-placement median remain required. Do not claim acceptance from any reported scratch result.'''\nd['changes'][0]['description']='Implement the 32-entry folded-PC snapshot-trained predictor as four unreset 16x1 data planes (two bit planes in each of two banks), one asynchronous logical read port and one synchronous write port. Use 32 reset-valid bits and logical default 01; write both state planes atomically before marking an entry valid. Eliminate training-state rereads and data-array resets. Capture complete raw logical counter snapshots in queue/bypass tokens, preserving pre-edge semantics. Retain direct targets, queue and correction behavior; verify RAM16 mapping.'\nd['changes'][-2]['description']+=' Include invalid-plane arbitrary contents, first writes, both bank boundaries and reset after populated storage; all invalid entries must immediately read logical 01.'\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=86));jsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nassert d['id']=='hyp-20261003-003-r13s2' and d['category']=='predictor'\nassert type(d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nprint('Schema valid;',len(d['changes']),'allowed change paths;',p.stat().st_size,'bytes')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
