{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_12", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id'] in ['hyp-20261003-003-r9s2','hyp-20261003-002-r9s1','hyp-20261003-001-r13s0']:\n  print(d['id']); print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261003-002-r9s1\nPartition conditional-branch resolution into registered static control in ID and dynamic operand comparisons in EX. At the existing ID/EX capture edge, register one-hot controls for the six legal branch predicates, one-hot controls for the predicate that means the captured prediction is wrong, branch-training eligibility derived from direct target alignment, and the single correction destination implied by the captured prediction. This is one structural retiming of the branch-control boundary; it neither adds a pipeline stage nor changes prediction policy, fetch buffering, forwarding selection, ALU/M service schedules or retirement width.\n\nFor a validated branch, form six outcome enables for EQ, NE, signed LT, signed GE, unsigned LT and unsigned GE. For an aligned direct target, form the corresponding six recovery enables after XORing branch_op bit zero with this token's predicted_taken bit. Thus a predicted-not-taken BEQ requests correction on EQ, while a predicted-taken BEQ requests correction on NE; the same complementary pairing applies to signed and unsigned comparisons. All other recovery enables are zero. For a misaligned direct target, actual_taken must be false whether or not the comparison succeeds, so record a separate forced-fallthrough recovery bit equal to predicted_taken. Keep default-illegal decoding unchanged; nonbranches and invalid decode entries must not acquire branch enables.\n\nAlso register two mutually exclusive training classes for legal branches: aligned target, which can train for either outcome, and misaligned target, which may train only if the condition is false. The latter preserves the existing rule that an untaken branch does not fault merely because its encoded target is misaligned. Compute the target alignment from the full-width PC-plus-immediate semantics in ID. Do not truncate architectural targets or wrap addresses. Register one branch_recovery_target alongside this metadata: predicted_taken ? PC+4 : PC+branch_immediate. A direction correction for a cond\n…[14929 of 18001 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:fb88031ed256921e]…\nths might dominate. Measure the prescribed vendor\nplacement median; the forecast is not a measured gain.\n\nA scratch prototype of this exact EX substitution and three-lane IF\nselection measured 73.689 MHz in vendor placement option 1, using 5,418\nLUT4, 1,929 registers, four BSRAMs and two DSPs. This is slightly BELOW\nthe champion and below the acceptance threshold, not a demonstrated gain.\nThe simpler EX-only precursor reached 73.283 MHz and passed the existing\nreal/ALTOPS pipeline suites, all eight selftest/random reference-ISS\ncomparisons with and without bus stalls, and canonical CoreMark at\n4,037,538 bracket cycles. That correctness evidence applies only to the\nprecursor. Extra EX target flattening, comparator rewrites, broad result\npredecode and a separate address register were slower and are excluded.\nThe five-percent estimate is a low-confidence goal for final physical\nmapping; the measured prototype does not establish it. Full prescribed\nmedian timing and unchanged correctness gates remain mandatory.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
