{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_56", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r14s2.yaml');s=p.read_text()\ns=s.replace('Pipeline training of a compact bias-relative one-bit predictor','One-hot pipelined learning for a compact agree predictor')\ns=s.replace('training event, capture a training-valid bit, folded index, exact outcome\\\\n  and immediate sign into a one-entry registered update pipeline. On the\\\\n  following edge, its valid update writes outcome XOR sign to the matching\\\\n  table entry. Accept a new update while writing the old one, so consecutive\\\\n  advancing branches never overwrite a pending update. This is a one-bit overwrite,','training event, decode the folded index into a 32-bit one-hot update mask\\\\n  and register that mask together with outcome XOR immediate sign inside\\\\n  IF. Register an all-zero mask when no branch trains. On the following\\\\n  edge, each entry with its registered mask bit set writes the registered\\\\n  disagreement bit. Accept a new update while writing the old one, so\\\\n  consecutive advancing branches never overwrite a pending update. This is a one-bit overwrite,')\ns=s.replace('observability. All training outputs describe the registered update,\\\\n  not the current live EX instruction. Existing branch_index wiring may retain six bits with','observability. EX training outputs keep their current-cycle meanings;\\\\n  only IF table updates are delayed. Existing branch_index wiring may retain six bits with')\ns=s.replace('Use exactly 32 resettable table state bits with one synchronous\\\\n  write and one asynchronous lookup.', 'Implement 32 separately declared resettable one-bit state flops in\\\\n  constant-index generate blocks. Each flop has its own registered update\\\\n  enable; there is no variable-index write statement. Select prediction\\\\n  through constant-index masked terms and a balanced OR tree, with the\\\\n  folded-PC equality decodes evaluated in parallel. Together with the\\\\n  32-bit update mask and one data bit this uses 65 state bits. Avoid the\\\\n  inferred RAM/reset-emulation topology observed in the scratch version.')\ns=s.replace('Reset clears both the update-valid register and table state.', 'Reset clears the update mask, update data and table state.')\ns=s.replace('and dmem readiness, then clear update-valid unless another branch','and dmem readiness, then clear the update mask unless another branch')\ns=s.replace('Register the complete once-per-advance training event, folded index,\\\\n      exact outcome and immediate-sign bias. Present the old update to IF\\\\n      while capturing the next event, clearing validity on idle cycles and\\\\n      reset. Preserve immediate recovery, traps, replay and M units.', 'Export the immediate-sign training bias and folded index alongside\\\\n      the unchanged current-cycle branch training event and exact outcome.\\\\n      Preserve immediate recovery, traps, replay and M units.')\ns=s.replace('outcome/bias overwrite training from the registered update. Preserve the queue, raw decode,','outcome/bias overwrite training via a registered one-hot mask and data.\\\\n      Use separately enabled constant-index state flops and a balanced\\\\n      masked-OR lookup instead of inferred RAM. Preserve the queue, raw decode,')\ns=s.replace('bias-relative one-bit writes delayed by one edge. Verify captured','bias-relative one-bit table writes delayed by one edge while EX event\\\\n      signals retain their current-cycle meaning. Verify captured')\ns=s.replace('  No implementation or timing claim is implied by\\\\n  this forecast;', '  No implementation or timing claim is implied by\\\\n  this forecast;')\ns=s.replace('  report final measured cycles and median clock explicitly.', '  report final measured cycles and median clock explicitly.')\nneedle='expected_impact:\\\\n'\nnote='''  Experimental limitation: an indexed-array precursor with registered\\\\n  training mapped to six RAM16 resources, used 5,076 LUT4 and 1,819\\\\n  registers, validated canonical CoreMark at 4,060,611 bracket cycles\\\\n  with no out-of-bounds accesses, and reached only 68.509 MHz in placement\\\\n  option 1. It is a regression, not winning evidence. Its unchanged\\\\n  branch-to-divider progress test passed, but moving the public internal\\\\n  branch_train event into a register caused reset-related pipeline tests\\\\n  to fail; the final design preserves that event and pipelines only IF\\\\n  learning. The proposed separately enabled state flops, one-hot update\\\\n  register and balanced lookup are an unmeasured implementation refinement\\\\n  addressing inferred RAM/reset logic. Full correctness and median timing\\\\n  remain required; do not report a demonstrated fitness improvement.\\\\n'''\ns=s.replace(needle,note+needle)\np.write_text(s)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
