{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_24", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id']=='hyp-20261003-002-r9s1':\n  print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis']); print(d['fmax_mhz'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Partition conditional-branch resolution into registered static control in ID and dynamic operand comparisons in EX. At the existing ID/EX capture edge, register one-hot controls for the six legal branch predicates, one-hot controls for the predicate that means the captured prediction is wrong, branch-training eligibility derived from direct target alignment, and the single correction destination implied by the captured prediction. This is one structural retiming of the branch-control boundary; it neither adds a pipeline stage nor changes prediction policy, fetch buffering, forwarding selection, ALU/M service schedules or retirement width.\n\nFor a validated branch, form six outcome enables for EQ, NE, signed LT, signed GE, unsigned LT and unsigned GE. For an aligned direct target, form the corresponding six recovery enables after XORing branch_op bit zero with this token's predicted_taken bit. Thus a predicted-not-taken BEQ requests correction on EQ, while a predicted-taken BEQ requests correction on NE; the same complementary pairing applies to signed and unsigned comparisons. All other recovery enables are zero. For a misaligned direct target, actual_taken must be false whether or not the comparison succeeds, so record a separate forced-fallthrough recovery bit equal to predicted_taken. Keep default-illegal decoding unchanged; nonbranches and invalid decode entries must not acquire branch enables.\n\nAlso register two mutually exclusive training classes for legal branches: aligned target, which can train for either outcome, and misaligned target, which may train only if the condition is false. The latter preserves the existing rule that an untaken branch does not fault merely because its encoded target is misaligned. Compute the target alignment from the full-width PC-plus-immediate semantics in ID. Do not truncate architectural targets or wrap addresses. Register one branch_recovery_target alongside this metadata: predicted_taken ? PC+4 : PC+branch_immediate. A direction correction for a conditional branch necessa\n…[3845 of 6917 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1dd7d1916418cec8]…\nuctural mechanism. Its timing benefit remains uncertain. Its final implementation must be judged by measured median vendor Fmax times actual iteration/cycle rate; ordinary ALU/divider timing and extra control fanout may prevent a win.\n\nRun the unchanged formal checks, full real/ALTOPS pipeline suites, stalled RVFI cosimulation and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/marker validation. Preserve the existing nine-cycle ready-bus branch-to-divider gap assertion and formal liveness window. Test every legal branch predicate and prediction direction, signed/unsigned boundaries, all forwarding sources, misaligned targets for taken and untaken outcomes, illegal branch encodings, JAL/JALR faults, canceled-write replay, independent bus stalls and reset. Require exact RVFI operands, trap/PC/order and once-only memory effects. Preserve nret=1, all public IO, every decoder/trap rule and bounded address requirement; do not change evaluation files or weaken checks. Deliver only this hypothesis with repository RTL unchanged.\n70.837\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
