{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_37", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r15s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261003-003-r15s2',\n'title':'Verify branch predictions before forwarding operand selection',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The current branch prediction verifier waits for two four-way 32-bit operand muxes before performing equality or ordering comparisons. Prior recovery predecode and registered recovery attempts did not clear the fitness threshold, and compact learned predictors lost Fmax. The winning r8s2 already supplies registered one-hot forwarding-source predictions. These masks can select a precomputed relation instead of feeding wide operand muxes ahead of the branch comparator. This keeps the useful predictor policy and removes serial selection from its verification datapath.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Keep the existing 64-entry two-bit direction predictor and all prediction/recovery timing, but verify branches by comparing candidate operand sources before forwarding selection. In EX, define four rs1 candidates {in.rs1_val, EX/MEM ALU, WB ALU, WB load} and four rs2 candidates {in.rs2_val, EX/MEM ALU, WB ALU, WB load}. For each source pair compute exact 32-bit equality, signed less-than and unsigned less-than in parallel. Select each relation using the conjunction of the already registered fwd_rs1_sel and fwd_rs2_sel bits, then reduce the 16 one-hot terms with balanced OR trees. Synthesis may share identical/self comparisons and signed/unsigned arithmetic, but must not refactor the circuit into wide selected operands ahead of one comparator. BEQ/BNE use the selected equality and its complement, BLT/BGE signed less-than and its complement, and BLTU/BGEU unsigned less-than and its complement.\n\nThis is one predictor-verification architecture: use the existing predicted operand source lanes to choose already evaluated branch relations. There is no additional prediction table, stale operand-value guess, speculative architectural result or extra verification stage. Retain the original forwarded rs1/rs2 datapaths for arithmetic, stores, JALR, M operations and RVFI. Use the exact selected relations consistently for branch outcome, predictor training, fault qualification, next-PC and correction, avoiding a second post-forwarding branch comparator that remains on a training path. Preserve full-width native comparison semantics, especially sign differences, INT_MIN and equality boundaries. Do not approximate comparisons with low bits or move correction later.\n\nThe registered source masks are one-hot for a live instruction whose operand permissions validate; reset/flush bubbles may have zero masks. Preserve source-mask generation and hold/drain transitions exactly. Canceled-producer prediction failures must still replay the original consumer PC, suppress EX advancement and training, and forbid M launch and younger side effects. Do not use a speculative relation when operand permissions fail. Keep all original generic EX-advance, replay and recovery qualifications; prove correctness under reachable pipeline states without new formal assumptions. Invalid zero-control entries never authorize branch training or redirection regardless of unselected relation values.\n\nPreserve the direction table, pre-edge lookup/update semantics, precise captured predicted_taken bit, two-entry queue, raw bus bypass, legal B/J predecode and full-width bounded immediate-derived target. Correct predictions retain their successor. Real corrections flush younger work on the current EX edge, override unready imem and wait during older dmem holds. Branches train once at their original advancement boundary. Keep load-use bubbles, all M-unit schedules, trap and link-write behavior, default-illegal decode, nret=1 IO, exact RVFI operands/PC/order and all memory side-effect discipline.\n\nThe expected benefit is shorter source-selection-to-recovery timing at unchanged prediction accuracy and cycle schedule. The cost is comparator duplication, higher source fanout and routing. Forecast 6 percent higher fitness with low confidence; this is not a measured improvement. At 4,037,538 bracket cycles, acceptance requires median Gowin Fmax above approximately 77.27 MHz and fitness above 191.37616 iterations/s. The unchanged arithmetic and divider paths may become limiting. Judge the actual median Fmax times CoreMark iterations/cycle, not comparator depth alone.\n\nRun existing real/ALTOPS pipeline and arithmetic suites, unchanged formal checks, reference-ISS cosimulation and canonical stalled CoreMark validation. Do not relax the existing nine-cycle branch-to-divider gap or formal liveness bounds. Add focused cases spanning all 16 source pairs, all six legal branch predicates, both saved prediction directions, equal and unequal operands, signed boundaries, competing writers, x0, invalidated producer replay, older dmem stalls and simultaneous imem stalls. Require exact post-forwarded RVFI values, targets/traps/order, once-only training and absence of wrong-path memory effects. Preserve all canonical CRC/UART/marker and bounded-address requirements.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Compute exact branch equality and signed/unsigned ordering for the 4-by-4 candidate operand source pairs in parallel. Select relations with the existing registered one-hot forwarding masks and balanced OR trees, then decode the branch predicate. Feed the exact result to existing verification, training and architectural outcome logic. Preserve other forwarding consumers, replay, EX acceptance, target arithmetic, traps and M units. Avoid synthesizing the original operand-mux-before-comparator topology.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Extend branch-prediction verification 