he existing 64-entry bimodal direction policy, direct target\n  calculation and range/alignment eligibility checks. Do not add a larger\n  direction table, BTB, return stack, load-value predictor or arithmetic changes.\n\n  Exempt only raw, positively decoded legal BRANCH encodings from the interlock\n  when the valid load currently in EX has a nonzero destination matching rs1\n  or rs2. The load must actually advance and the branch must actually be\n  accepted before any deferred state is captured. All other load consumers\n  retain the existing interlock. Alongside the accepted branch, latch a\n  deferred-verification bit and two source-needs-load bits. Keep the existing\n  predicted_taken bit; direct targets still derive from this branch's own\n  instruction and PC. Imem unready, older dmem holds, divider waits, reset and\n  flush retain their normal acceptance priorities. No prediction is evidence\n  that an unready load has completed.\n\n  In EX, a deferred branch does not resolve, redirect, train, or apply a\n  conditional-target misalignment trap using unavailable operands. Carry its\n  branch operation, target, prediction, pending-source mask and forwarded\n  operands into EX/MEM. Ordinary branches and JAL/JALR retain EX resolution.\n  For a pending source, explicitly reject the older load's EX/MEM address\n  as a forwarded value. Capture a fallback operand using forwarding from\n  older completed writers or the ID/EX source value, excluding that pending\n  load. In particular, retain the older MEM/WB writer's value when applicable.\n  This fallback is needed if the load eventually traps and suppresses its\n  register write; do not substitute a faulting load's data or effective address.\n\n  In MEM, the preceding load has reached MEM/WB. For each pending source,\n  use its completed, sign/zero-extended WB value only when the WB instruction\n  actually writes the matching nonzero register; otherwise use the captured\n  fallback. Resolve the branch condition and actual next PC from these exact\n  operands, applying the existing taken-target misalignment trap policy.\n  Patch the branch's MEM/WB RVFI source values, actual pc_next and trap fields\n  accordingly. Never retire a predicted outcome or an unresolved branch.\n  Older dmem stalls hold the branch in EX until the load is accepted, preserving\n  the current retained MEM/WB forwarding behavior. Once the branch occupies\n  MEM it has no data-memory request and cannot wait on io_dmemReady.\n\n  A correct prediction lets the younger EX instruction advance normally.\n  On a late mismatch, redirect to the actual branch target or PC+4, flush\n  fetch/ID, and kill the younger instruction currently in EX by inserting a\n  zero-control invalid EX/MEM entry. The late correction is older and must\n  override any simultaneous younger EX correction, branch feedback, load-use\n  indication or execute_wait. Gate divider start and result acceptance for\n  the squashed younger instruction and ensure its execute_wait cannot block\n  the squash. Because the deferred branch is immediately ahead of that\n  instruction, a younger division cannot have launched before this check;\n  prevent its same-edge launch rather than letting wrong-path divider state\n  persist. Do not kill the resolving branch's MEM/WB entry or its older load.\n  Younger stores have not reached MEM and must never issue a memory request.\n  Correction still overrides an unready instruction bus.\n\n  Keep a single predictor write port by moving all conditional-branch training\n  to MEM advancement. Ordinary branches carry their EX-computed outcome;\n  deferred branches supply the outcome verified in MEM. Train the current\n  counter at the branch's own PC exactly once only for a valid, legal,\n  non-faulting branch. This avoids two simultaneous table writes when a late\n  branch is followed by an ordinary branch. Do not train killed younger work,\n  held entries, JAL/JALR or bubbles. Preserve pre-edge lookup/update semantics;\n  accept that regular-branch training is one cycle later, without a bypass\n  from MEM comparison to fetch prediction. Keep predictor state nonarchitectural.\n\n  The forecast is a low-confidence 5% fitness gain, aiming for approximately\n  2.5% fewer cycles together with approximately 2.5% higher median Fmax.\n  The trace suggests at most about 128,121 net saved issue slots before bus\n  overlap and predictor-update timing, since a late miss costs an extra\n  younger slot. It does not establish a 5% cycle gain. A measured result near\n  4,100,000 cycles would need median Fmax above 49.083 MHz to exceed 119.7147\n  iterations/s, the champion plus 4.6%. This clock increase is unproven; late\n  correction fanout, additional metadata and placement could instead lower\n  Fmax. Keep the new comparator separate from arithmetic and existing direct\n  branch recovery, and avoid adding wide predicted-PC comparison or a new\n  load-data-to-EX combinational forwarding path. Evaluate the actual product\n  with vendor timing rather than claiming acceptance from predictor accuracy.\n\n  Preserve nret=1, every core port, decoder legality, full architectural\n  address arithmetic, trap/link semantics, contiguous RVFI retirement order,\n  and the eight-service-edge divider schedule. Run existing unit, formal and\n  stalled cosimulation gates and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/marker checks.\n  Specifically retain the unchanged formal liveness window: a late correction\n  immediately followed by DIV/REM must still make progress without relaxing\n  a checker, depth or evaluation contract.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Recognize the legal raw conditional-branch exception to a genuine\n      nonzero load-use dependency. Exempt only that case, retaining all other\n      interlocks and bus/divider holds. Export the source dependency mask for\n      accepted branch metadata. Give an older late correction priority over\n      younger EX execute_wait and flush its ID/EX slot without holding stale work.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: |\n      Add deferred-branch and pending-load-source metadata to ID/EX and EX/MEM.\n      Carry the original prediction and verified ordinary branch outcome to\n      MEM as needed. Reuse existing PC, target and operand fields where possible;\n      keep every architectural RVFI field and retirement width unchanged.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Capture deferred-verification and source masks only on an accepted\n      branch paired with an advancing older load. Hold them with the complete\n      instruction on backpressure and clear them on invalid fetch/reset/flush.\n      Preserve raw instruction decode and existing operand capture semantics.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      For deferred branches, capture correct fallback operands while excluding\n      the pending load's address from forwarding, and pass unresolved branch\n      metadata to MEM. Suppress their early condition-based correction/trap.\n      Retain normal branch/JAL/JALR resolution. Add older-late-kill handling\n      that zeroes younger EX/MEM side effects and gates divider launch/acceptance\n      and younger corrections. Carry ordinary branch outcomes to MEM for training.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Add deferred branch verification using the matching actual WB write value\n      and captured fallback operands. Produce late correction/target and the\n      single once-per-advancement branch-training stream for all conditional\n      branches. Correct MEM/WB branch operands, next-PC and trap metadata before\n      retirement. Keep ordinary load extraction, stores and WB-hold behavior.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Wire legal branch/load dependency metadata, WB verification values, MEM\n      predictor training and late correction. Arbitrate correction by age and\n      wire the younger EX kill independently of the resolving branch's progress.\n      Preserve the top-level IO and sole channel-0 retirement contract.\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Accept the unified MEM-stage branch-training stream and the age-selected\n      correction while retaining the exact 64x2 predictor, immediate-derived\n      targets, target eligibility, pre-edge updates and PC priority. A late\n      correction overrides a held or unavailable fetch just as EX correction does.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Add cycle-sensitive correctly predicted load-to-branch cases proving the\n      issue bubble disappears for LB/LBU/LH/LHU/LW and either or both source\n      dependencies. Test both late correction directions, forwarded fallback\n      values after faulting loads, target misalignment, wrong-path stores and\n      DIV/REM, adjacent normal/deferred branches and simultaneous corrections.\n      Cover long dmem holds, imem stalls, reset, x0, reserved encodings, one-time\n      MEM predictor training and exact RVFI operands/PCs/traps/orders. Include\n      a late misprediction followed by DIV/REM within the unchanged liveness\n      bound. Keep all existing assertions and update EX-specific training\n      observations to the defined MEM training boundary.\n  - file: test/test_hazard_unit.py\n    description: |\n      Cover the precise branch-only load-use exemption, source masks and age\n      priority under late correction, raw wrong-path dependencies, imem/dmem\n      stalls and execute_wait. Assert that every other load consumer still\n      receives its required interlock and held live instructions remain intact.\n''')\nimport json, yaml, jsonschema\nh=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\njsonschema.validate(h,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nassert h['id']=='hyp-20261003-003-r4s2' and h['category']=='predictor'\nassert type(h['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nassert -50 <= h['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct'] <= 50\nprint('Schema valid:',p)\nprint('Changes:',len(h['changes']))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Schema valid: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r4s2.yaml\nChanges: 9\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
