{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='predictor':\n  print('\\\\n', d['id'],d['title'])\n  print({k:d.get(k) for k in ('fitness','cycles','fmax_mhz','outcome','critical_path')})\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  if d['id'] \"'!= '\"'hyp-20261003-003-r8s2':\n   print(h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\n hyp-20261003-003-r1s2 Fetch-stage bimodal prediction with immediate-derived targets\n{'fitness': 12.75, 'cycles': 4201766, 'fmax_mhz': 5.359, 'outcome': 'regression', 'critical_path': {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.ctrl.reg_write_s0', 'to': 'dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -195.924, 'arrival_ns': 206.219, 'logic_cells': 148, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}}\nAdd one compact fetch-stage next-PC predictor: a 64-entry, two-bit\nsaturating bimodal direction table indexed by PC[7:2], combined with\ntargets decoded directly from the fetched B/J immediate. Initialize all\ncounters to weakly not-taken (01); their MSB predicts conditional-branch\ndirection. Recognize only legal BRANCH funct3 values and JAL. Predict JAL\ntaken unconditionally when its target is eligible; JALR and all other\ninstructions predict PC+4. Use full 32-bit PC-relative arithmetic and\nrestrict speculative taken targets to word-aligned addresses in main\nmemory [0x00000000, 0x00100000). An ineligible target predicts fall-through\nand is resolved normally in EX. Keep the table inside if_stage.sv, with\n128 counter bits and no tags, target array, global history, or return stack.\n\nForm predictions from the raw imem_data and fetch PC, independently of\nthe flush-masked IF/ID instruction, to avoid combinational feedback.\nCarry the exact predicted next PC with the instruction through IF/ID\nand ID/EX. Only apply a prediction when the instruction is accepted:\nimem is ready, no load-use/data-memory hold exists, and no older EX\ncorrection squashes it. Prediction itself must not flush its instruction\nor its correctly predicted successor. Hold the captured prediction with\nthe rest of ID/EX during data-memory stalls.\n\nIn EX, compute resolved_next_pc using the existing forwarded comparison,\nJAL/JALR targets, and misalignment/trap behavior. Change redirect to\nin.valid && !stall && (resolved_next_pc != in.predicted_next_pc), and use\nresolved_next_pc as the correction target. This recovers both predicted\nnot-taken/actually-taken and predicted \n…[34191 of 37263 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7d292cd6ec100238]…\nl measurement. At 2% more cycles the\nmedian Gowin clock must exceed approximately 61.40 MHz to beat the\nchampion by 4.6%, and approximately 62.22 MHz to gain 6%. This requires\na physical clock improvement, not an accuracy claim. The existing\nALU-to-memory path may remain critical and defeat the hypothesis.\nRun unchanged unit, formal, stalled cosimulation and canonical\nCoreMark CRC/UART/marker checks, then compare median vendor Fmax times\niterations/cycle. Preserve nret=1, IO, decoder legality, trap/link\nsemantics, contiguous RVFI order and the unchanged formal progress\nwindow, including a corrected transfer followed by DIV/REM.\n\n\n hyp-20261003-003-r8s2 Predict forwarding sources and WB result kind before execute\n{'fitness': 182.96, 'cycles': 4037538, 'fmax_mhz': 73.869, 'outcome': 'improvement', 'critical_path': {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_fwd/fwd_rs1_3_s1', 'slack_ns': -9.691, 'arrival_ns': 19.985, 'logic_cells': 42, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_id']}}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
