{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_15", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id']=='hyp-20261003-003-r5s2':\n  print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\n if d.get('category')=='predictor':\n  for k,v in d.items():\n   if isinstance(v,str) and any(x in v.lower() for x in ['51,857','529,588','return','trace']):\n    if k not in ('title','motivation','lesson'): print(d['id'], k, v[:4000])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Use the existing bimodal prediction to issue an immediately load-dependent\nconditional branch without its load-use bubble. Defer only the condition\ncheck to a small branch verification sidecar parallel to MEM. This is\none predictor mechanism: speculation across load-to-branch latency with\nmandatory verification and squash before younger architectural effects.\nPreserve the existing prediction table, direct targets, fetch FIFO,\ndivider schedule, arithmetic and nret=1 contract.\n\nAdmit only a valid positively decoded legal BRANCH whose rs1 and/or rs2\nmatches the advancing valid load's nonzero destination. Capture a pending\nsource mask with that branch on actual ID acceptance. All other consumers\nretain the existing interlock. Older data-memory or divider holds continue\nto hold the branch normally; instruction-bus stalls cannot create an\naccepted instruction. Preserve the exact fetched predicted_taken bit.\n\nIn EX, a marked branch neither verifies its condition nor trains or\nredirects. Carry its PC, direct target, comparison operation, prediction,\npending mask and correct fallback operands to a narrow sidecar registered\non the branch's EX advancement. Reuse existing EX/MEM PC, target and\nsource fields instead of duplicating wide architectural payloads; the\nadditional logical sidecar fields are the deferred flag, source mask,\nprediction and comparison operation. Reusing source/target fields still\nmakes formerly RVFI-only registers and routes part of the timed circuit;\naccount for that area and routing cost. Exclude the preceding load's effective\naddress from pending-source forwarding. Retain the freshest older value\nfor each pending source, including WB forwarding, in case the load traps\nand does not write. Ordinary branches and jumps still resolve in EX.\n\nWhen the sidecar is valid, the older load is in MEM/WB. Select its actual\nsign/zero-extended value only if that load writes the matching nonzero\nregister; otherwise use the captured fallback. Resolve the condition and\ntaken-target misalignment with full architectural \n…[2707 of 5779 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a296b3e4df9b338a]…\nn across arbitrarily long memory stalls.\n\nForecast a low-confidence 6% fitness improvement, with approximately\n3% fewer cycles plus modest clock recovery from the isolated squash\ncontrols. Neither component is measured on this champion. A cycle\nsaving alone may miss the 4.6% acceptance threshold, and the new feedback\ncontrol could instead lower Fmax. Acceptance requires measured median\nGowin Fmax in Hz times 10/Cnew above 126.07438 iter/s. At 3% fewer\ncycles this needs more than 49.0414 MHz, versus the champion's 48.333\nMHz. The earlier validity-separation attempt r3s1 reached 49.295 MHz,\nsupporting plausibility but not predicting timing for this new circuit.\nThe architectural trace gives roughly 128,122 saved issue slots minus\noverlap and delayed-training effects, after charging an extra slot for\neach late mismatch; it does not establish a 6% cycle saving. Run unchanged unit,\nformal, stalled cosimulation, CoreMark CRC/UART and marker checks;\npreserve all IO, decoder, trap, ordering and liveness invariants.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
