{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_64","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom tools.eval.gowin import build_all,summarize\np=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/561ff4c6/d7911b0f/predecoded_recovery')\nr=build_all(Path.cwd(),p/'rtl','fpga/core_bench_si.sv',p/'timing')\nprint(summarize(r),flush=True)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{'placement_failed': False, 'fmax_mhz': 72.154, 'seeds': [71.018, 72.154, 72.154], 'perturbations': [[0, 71.018, 17], [1, 72.154, 17], [2, 72.154, 17]], 'lut4': 5304, 'ff': 1933, 'lutram': 0, 'bsram': 4, 'dsp': 2, 'logic_levels': 17, 'critical_path': {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_div/remainder_6_s1', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_div/remainder_2_s1', 'slack_ns': -9.081, 'arrival_ns': 19.375, 'logic_cells': 61, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_div']}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_69", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r9s2.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Predecode prediction recovery predicates before execute'\nd['hypothesis']='''Keep the existing 64-entry bimodal predictor and same-cycle EX recovery,\nbut move prediction-dependent recovery decoding to the ID/EX boundary.\nRegister four mutually exclusive verification enables: expect equality,\nexpect inequality, expect less-than, and expect not-less-than. Derive the\nexpected primitive result as predicted_taken XOR branch funct3 bit 0;\nBEQ/BNE use equality and the four ordered branches use less-than. Enable\nthese checks only for a positively decoded legal conditional branch with\nan aligned direct target. Target alignment is exactly the low two bits\nof PC plus immediate; retain full-width target arithmetic everywhere\nthat actually constructs an address. Capture a separate direct-JAL\ncorrection bit for legal aligned JAL whose captured prediction is false.\nThis is predecoded prediction verification, with no new prediction table,\nbranch latency, deferred recovery, or speculative architectural result.\n\nIn EX, use exact existing forwarded operands to compute one equality\nand one unsigned less-than relation. Signed ordering uses rs1[31] when\nsigns differ and unsigned less-than otherwise; branch funct3 selects the\nsigned versus unsigned interpretation. Let the registered verification\nenables directly select the violated primitive relations with parallel\nAND/OR terms. OR this result with the registered JAL-correction bit and\nthe legal, aligned JALR correction, then apply existing EX-advancement\nqualification and operand-permission replay priority. Remove the generic\nactual_taken-versus-predicted_taken comparison from the global correction\ncone. Instruction classification, expected outcome, direct-target\nalignment and direct-JAL eligibility must not be decoded serially after\nthe operand comparison. Retain native full-width comparison mapping:\na scratch byte-sliced comparator instead reached only 62.743 MHz median\nat unchanged cycles, so the proposal does not prescribe that topology.\n\nDerive actual branch condition, training outcome and RVFI next PC from\nthe same exact relations with the original funct3 inversion. Architectural\noutcome/trap logic remains fully checked but does not feed the redundant\nlate generic correction comparison. The fetch design already guarantees\nthat predicted_taken is true only for legal aligned direct transfers\nwhose complete target lies in main memory; JALR always arrives predicted\nfalse. Prove and test these metadata invariants rather than introducing\nan assumption into formal. They justify treating JALR as an always-missed\naligned legal jump and suppressing direct checks for misaligned targets.\nA taken misaligned branch/JAL/JALR still traps and suppresses link writes\nas today; its architectural successor is PC+4. Never redirect to a\nmisaligned target or change the existing full-width fetch range checks.\n\nCapture all verification bits from the selected queue token and that\ntoken's saved predicted_taken, never a fresh counter lookup. Hold them\nwith the entire ID/EX token across dmem and M-unit waits, and preserve\nexisting reset, flush and invalid-bubble clearing exactly. Keep current\nforwarding masks, canceled-write replay, load-use interlocks, complete\nID/EX squash, EX/MEM advancement and M schedules. Replay overrides branch\nrecovery and forbids training and M launch as today. Only valid legal\nadvancing branches train, exactly once; keep training in EX, including\npre-edge lookup/update semantics. Correct predictions retain younger\nwork; correction flushes on the current EX edge even with imem unready.\n\nThis specifically avoids the earlier all-branch deferred recovery cost\nof 1.64% extra cycles. A scratch selective ordered-branch deferred design\nstill reached only 66.751 MHz despite reducing that cost to 0.49%, so\nno delayed-verification mechanism is included in this proposal. Focus\ninstead on moving recovery eligibility and expected-relation selection\nbefore the existing register boundary, at an unchanged cycle schedule.\n\nForecast 6% fitness improvement with low confidence, from higher Fmax.\nAt the champion's 4,037,538 cycles, acceptance requires median vendor\nFmax above approximately 77.27 MHz and fitness above 191.37616 iter/s;\n6% requires about 78.30 MHz. Prediction accuracy is unchanged. Placement,\nnew control registers and the next arithmetic critical path are material\nrisks; a shallower recovery cone is not itself evidence of acceptance.\nMeasure all three prescribed placement options and the actual product.\n\nPreserve nret=1, external IO, default-illegal decode, exact traps, RVFI\noperands/next-PC/order, bounded addresses, all canonical CoreMark CRCs,\nUART validation and marker timing. Keep all existing unit assertions,\nincluding cleared ID/EX and zero source masks after squash, the original\nbranch-to-divider latency bound and formal liveness window. Run unchanged\nreal/ALTOPS pipeline tests, formal, stalled cosimulation and canonical\nCoreMark validation. Add focused relation/prediction coverage without\nweakening checks or modifying evaluation files.\n'''\nd['changes'][0]['description']='Add four one-hot prediction-verification enables and a direct-JAL correction bit to id_ex_t. Preserve predicted_taken, validity and all existing architectural/RVFI metadata.'\nd['changes'][1]['description']='Predecode expected primitive relation, branch classification, direct-target alignment and JAL correction eligibility from the selected instruction and its saved prediction. Capture the complete verification metadata with ID/EX under unchanged reset, flush, invalid and hold priorities.'\nd['changes'][2]['description']='Use shared exact equality and less-than relations with registered verification enables to form a shallow parallel direction-mismatch network. Combine it with predecoded direct-JAL correction and existing legal aligned JALR resolution, preserving EX qualification and replay priority. Retain native comparator mapping, actual branch/trap/RVFI outcome computation and once-only EX training; remove unused generic correction-only logic. Keep all arithmetic, forwarding, stage timing and side-effect suppression intact.'\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Updated and schema-validated',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
