{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_76","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r9s2.yaml');d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['hypothesis']=d['hypothesis'].replace('then apply existing EX-advancement\\\\nqualification and operand-permission replay priority.', '''then apply a specialized control-transfer acceptance qualification and\noperand-permission replay priority. The specialized qualification is\nin.valid AND \"'!stall AND !prediction_failed AND !reset. The verified\ninstruction classes cannot be MUL/DIV/REM, so the generic execute_wait\nand M-busy-dependent operands_invalid terms are unnecessary in this\nparticular correction path. Retain the original generic EX advancement,\nM-start validation and replay logic elsewhere. Prove equivalence under\nreachable pipeline states; do not add assumptions about busy or decode.'\"''')\nd['hypothesis'] += '''\nA scratch version with the predecoded predicates but still using generic\nEX-advancement qualification passed all 53 unchanged formal checks,\nall 37 existing pipeline tests in each real/ALTOPS mode, and canonical\nstalled CoreMark validation at 4,037,538 cycles. It measured\n71.018/72.154/72.154 MHz, median 72.154 MHz, with 5,304 LUT4 and 1,933\nregisters. This is approximately 178.71 iterations/s, BELOW the champion\nand acceptance threshold; it is not evidence of a demonstrated gain.\nThe specialized control-transfer qualification is an additional concrete\nrefinement beyond that tested version. The forecast is uncertain and\nrequires the implementation phase's full correctness and timing gates.\n'''\nd['changes'][2]['description'] += ' Use a control-transfer-specific valid/no-stall/no-prediction-failure/no-reset qualification instead of putting M execution-wait decoding on the correction cone. Prove it equivalent for the positively decoded non-M instruction classes; preserve all generic EX and M advancement conditions elsewhere.'\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Hypothesis saved and valid.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
